pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwAnimalPlantColour a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Animal/Plant/Colour"@en, "Tier/Pflanze/Farbe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group exercise: everyone studies the others for a few minutes and assigns each person an animal, a plant and a colour felt to suit them; each then reads out their list in turn. It can lead into a discussion of how the attributions relate to the four elements and other symbolic correspondences."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Animal/Plant/Colour, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwAnimalPlantColourMatchingOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Matching attributions in Animal/Plant/Colour"@en, "Übereinstimmende Zuordnungen bei Tier/Pflanze/Farbe"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the author's course, the attributions different people made for the same person were occasionally strikingly alike."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, not as a sign announced in advance: on the course, the animal, plant and colour that different people gave the same person were occasionally remarkably alike. Nothing is said of how often, or of what else might explain the likeness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Animal/Plant/Colour, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwStoriesAboutPassersBy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Inventing stories about passers-by"@en, "Geschichten über Vorübergehende erfinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit in a public place, look at a passer-by for a few seconds, then try to make up a story of what their life is like based only on that first glimpse; this shows how much our reading of others is tinted by our own habits and beliefs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Animal/Plant/Colour, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwInferenceFromAGlanceSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surprising amount inferred from a glance"@en, "Überraschend viel aus einem Blick erschlossen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reader is told they may be surprised how much detail they can infer about a stranger from a quick look."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of the passers-by exercise, the reader's surprise at how much can be inferred about a stranger from one glance; announced in advance with 'may', and nothing is given to check the inferences against."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Animal/Plant/Colour, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwAttendingToOthersWithoutOwnAttitudes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attending to others while setting aside one's own attitudes"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit für andere unter Zurückstellung eigener Haltungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paying attention to other people and being able to put one's own attitudes aside, described as an important skill for anyone who works with others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Animal/Plant/Colour, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwPassersByStoriesYieldAttendingToOthers a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Stories about passers-by train attention to others"@en, "Geschichten über Passanten schulen die Aufmerksamkeit für andere"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise of inventing lives for strangers is offered to show how our reading of others is coloured by our own habits, leading into the skill of attending to people while setting one's own attitudes aside."@en ;
    skos:note "The link is made by the paragraph, which puts the exercise and the skill side by side; no outcome is reported."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwStoriesAboutPassersBy ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwAttendingToOthersWithoutOwnAttitudes ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Animal/Plant/Colour, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwStrainingToSeeAurasFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Straining concentration fails to show auras"@en, "Angestrengte Konzentration zeigt keine Auren"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the story a young man spent much time concentrating hard on seeing tree auras, with little success."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of seeing auras by hard concentration on something physical; in the story a young man spends much time trying this with little success. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the method, effortful looking, and the story turns to success once he imagines instead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Seeing Auras, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwImaginingAnAuraIntoView a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagining an aura into perception"@en, "Eine Aura in die Wahrnehmung hinein imaginieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "From an old story Hine tells: instead of straining to see a tree's aura, consider the tree and wonder what its aura would look like if one could see it, letting colours and edges suggest themselves, until one realises that the impression is the aura."@en ;
    skos:note "Taken from a story Hine calls old, about an unnamed young man; no source is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Seeing Auras, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwRowanAuraAppearsOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The rowan's aura appears"@en, "Die Aura der Eberesche erscheint"@de ;
    skos:definition "While picturing what a rowan's aura might look like (golden russet-brown with yellow edges), the young man suddenly realised he was actually seeing it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, not as a sign announced in advance: in the story, picturing a rowan's aura in golden russet-brown with yellow edges, the young man suddenly realises he is seeing it. The seeing is identified with the impression itself, so the report cannot separate it from imagining."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Seeing Auras, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwImaginingAuraYieldsSeeingAuras a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Imagining the aura yields seeing it"@en, "Die Aura imaginieren führt zum Aurasehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the story, wondering what a tree's aura would look like leads to the realisation that it is being seen."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwImaginingAnAuraIntoView ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSeeingAuras ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Seeing Auras, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSeeingAuras a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing auras"@en, "Auren sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving auras, understood not as seeing something physical but as opening the mind to impressions, which we usually render as visual images such as colours, though other senses can serve as well."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondASensingAuras (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node lists sensing auras among the so-called siddhis, as the fruit of long practice; here seeing an aura is not seeing anything physical but opening the mind to impressions, which sight-dominated people render as colour although other senses could serve."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Seeing Auras, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSeeingWhatWeExpectCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "We see what we expect"@en, "Wir sehen, was wir erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author reminds that we often perceive what we expect to be there rather than what is actually present."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSeeingAuras ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sight Exercises, Seeing Auras, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .



#
# Sound Exercises
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSelectiveHearing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Selective hearing"@en, "Selektives Hören"@de ;
    skos:definition "We spend more effort screening sounds out than listening; the brain learns to sort significant noises from harmless ones (soldiers sleeping through a barrage but waking at a rifle bolt nearby)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwActiveListening a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Active Listening"@en, "Aktives Zuhören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit in a room with a steady repetitive background sound such as a ticking clock. While busy with something else the sound will drop below awareness; repeat daily until you can keep the background noise in awareness without losing it and without straining to concentrate on it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSustainedBackgroundSoundAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxed sustained awareness of background sound"@en, "Entspanntes anhaltendes Gewahrsein von Hintergrundgeräuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding a background noise in awareness continuously without either losing it or concentrating fiercely upon it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwActiveListeningYieldsSustainedAwareness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Active Listening yields relaxed awareness of background sound"@en, "Aktives Zuhören führt zu entspanntem Gewahrsein von Hintergrundgeräuschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeating the exercise daily is the route given to keeping a background noise in awareness without strain."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwActiveListening ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSustainedBackgroundSoundAwareness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwBackgroundSoundHeldWithoutStrainSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Background noise held without strain"@en, "Hintergrundgeräusch ohne Anstrengung gehalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise is complete when the noise stays in awareness neither slipping away nor needing fierce concentration; the slipping of the noise below awareness while occupied is the sign it has not yet been reached."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of active listening, the background noise held in awareness without being lost and without fierce concentration; its slipping below awareness marks the stage not yet reached. Self-assessed; no duration is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGenuineListening a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Genuine listening to others"@en, "Echtes Zuhören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Real attention to what others say, important in dealing with people."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwCatchingOneselfNotListening a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Catching oneself not listening"@en, "Sich beim Nicht-Zuhören ertappen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In conversation, notice when you only seem to listen while actually waiting for the other to finish so you can say your piece; catching yourself at it is called a valuable lesson."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwCatchingNotListeningYieldsGenuineListening a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Catching oneself not listening teaches listening"@en, "Sich beim Nicht-Zuhören ertappen lehrt Zuhören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Noticing that one only waits for the other to finish is called a valuable lesson for dealing with people."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwCatchingOneselfNotListening ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGenuineListening ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Active Listening, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwHummingMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Humming Meditation"@en, "Summmeditation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group sits in a circle with eyes closed; each member hums at their own pitch with no rhythm to keep, resting when they wish; continue for at least 15 minutes, then discuss what happened."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Humming Meditation, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoundConcentration a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sound Concentration"@en, "Klangkonzentration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit comfortably and repeat a chosen word or phrase, first aloud and then silently."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicOrcOnePointedFocusing (Oven-Ready Chaos, 1992): the 1992 node lists mantra-yoga among several one-pointed techniques without a procedure; here the procedure is a single chosen word or phrase, said aloud and then silently, until the repeating seems to go on by itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Sound Concentration, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwOnePointedness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One-pointedness"@en, "Einspitzigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state of one-pointed concentration; plain repetition of a chosen word or phrase is called among the easiest and most effective ways into it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Sound Concentration, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoundConcentrationYieldsOnePointedness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sound concentration yields one-pointedness"@en, "Klangkonzentration führt zur Einspitzigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simply repeating a chosen word or phrase is named one of the easiest and most effective roads into one-pointedness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoundConcentration ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwOnePointedness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Sound Concentration, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoundRepeatsItselfSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The sound repeats itself"@en, "Der Klang wiederholt sich selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a while one stops being aware of repeating, and it may seem that the sound is no longer repeated by oneself but repeats itself through one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of sound concentration, losing awareness of repeating, so that the sound seems no longer to be said by oneself but to say itself through one. Self-perceived; no time is named beyond after a while."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Sound Concentration, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwFeelingMusic a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling Music"@en, "Musik fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Alone or in a group, use any relaxation technique, then listen to a taped piece of music, trying to feel it across the body and noticing whether images or even smells arise in the mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Feeling Music, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwEnhancedListening a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced listening"@en, "Verfeinertes Hören"@de ;
    skos:definition "An improved ability to listen, which music-based exercises are said to enhance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Sound Exercises, Feeling Music, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwFeelingMusicYieldsEnhancedListening a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling Music enhances listening"@en, "Musik fühlen verfeinert das Hören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using music, alone or in a group, is offered as one way to enhance the ability to listen."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwFeelingMusic ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwEnhancedListening ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
