#
# Smell Exercises
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwEvocativePowerOfSmell a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evocative power of smell"@en, "Evokative Kraft des Geruchs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Smell is called our least understood sense yet a direct line to memory and desire; hospitals are said to use 'coma kits' of strong synthetic smells to rouse coma patients; pheromones are said to carry subliminal signals of fear, pain, pleasure and various diseases, and may explain the aura of fear or peace some people carry; the bereaved often report smelling a lost partner as a comforting presence."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSmellHotlineMemory (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node gives smell a key role in magic as a direct line to memory; here the claim is set among hospital coma kits, pheromones that may carry fear, pain, pleasure and illness and explain the aura some people have, and the bereaved who smell a lost partner as a comforting presence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwNoticingSmellsAndBodyOdour a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Noticing smells and body odour"@en, "Gerüche und Körpergeruch beachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make a deliberate effort to notice odours and how they may affect your behaviour; also pay attention to the smell of your own body, which changes over time with diet and general health."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpiritsAnnouncedBySmell a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits announce themselves by smell"@en, "Geister kündigen sich durch Geruch an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many spirits are said to make their presence known through a sudden rush of odour; strange smells are also said to accompany UFO encounters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwMemoryImageAssociation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Memory/Image Association"@en, "Erinnerungs-/Bild-Assoziation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Have someone put a range of aromatic substances (e.g. essential oils) into unlabelled containers; relaxed, sniff each in turn, let memories and images arise, and follow each image the smell calls up."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBuildingPersonalScentCorrespondences (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice observes which memories scents call up in order to build a private table of correspondences; here the exercise is the blind sniffing itself, unlabelled containers prepared by someone else and each evoked image pursued."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, Memory/Image Association, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSmellEvokedMemoryAndImagery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Smell-evoked memory and imagery"@en, "Geruchsgeweckte Erinnerung und Bilder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calling up memories and images through scent, which the association exercise is said to demonstrate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, Memory/Image Association, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwMemoryImageAssociationYieldsEvokedMemory a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Memory/Image Association shows smell-evoked memory"@en, "Erinnerungs-/Bild-Assoziation zeigt geruchsgeweckte Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sniffing unlabelled aromatics while relaxed is said to demonstrate the evocative power of smell by letting memories and images rise."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwMemoryImageAssociation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSmellEvokedMemoryAndImagery ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, Memory/Image Association, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwPersonalAromaticCorrespondences a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal aromatic correspondences"@en, "Persönliche Duftentsprechungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A self-built set of scent attributions, said to be very useful for making one's own incense or for using scents in healing or trance."@en ;
    skos:note "Called a Smellphabet in this book; the practice of building it is carried by pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBuildingPersonalScentCorrespondences (Condensed Chaos, 1995)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, Building up a Smellphabet, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSmellphabetYieldsPersonalAromatics a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Building a Smellphabet yields personal aromatic correspondences"@en, "Ein Geruchsalphabet ergibt persönliche Duftentsprechungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working out one's own attributions of perfumes and incenses, instead of relying on someone else's, gives a set useful for making incense and for aromatics in healing or trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondBBuildingPersonalScentCorrespondences ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwPersonalAromaticCorrespondences ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Smell Exercises, Building up a Smellphabet, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .



#
# Space Exercises
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwPersonalSpaceAndConfidence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal space and confidence"@en, "Persönlicher Raum und Selbstvertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Besides inner space (visualisation, trance, dream), shamanic magic is said to need a sense of outer space and personal territory; the closeness we allow indicates intimacy; standards differ by culture (illustrated by an anecdote of Arabs and American tourists in Cairo); anxious people contract their bodies while confident people extend their space."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBBodySpaceReflectsProjectsMood (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node treats the use of personal space as mirroring and projecting mood in ritual posture; here personal space is the measure of intimacy we allow, differs by culture (the Cairo hostel anecdote of Arabs and American tourists), and matters for working with others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwRespectPersonalSpaceCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Respect others' personal space"@en, "Den persönlichen Raum anderer achten"@de ;
    skos:definition "When working with others, and especially in healing, one must acknowledge and be sensitive to people's differing sense of personal space and know when to keep back and when to come closer."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwPersonalSpaceAndConfidence ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwObservingEmpathisingAssessingOthers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Observing, empathising and intuitively assessing others"@en, "Andere beobachten, einfühlen und intuitiv einschätzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sharpened ability to watch, feel with and intuitively judge other people, on which knowing the right distance in healing is said to depend."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpaceAsSeparationTrap a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Space as separation is a perceptual trap"@en, "Raum als Trennung ist eine Wahrnehmungsfalle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordinary perception treats space as what separates and insulates us from things and people; this is called a trap one can outgrow by experiencing space differently."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGroupExplorationOfPersonalSpace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Group exploration of personal space"@en, "Gruppenerkundung des persönlichen Raums"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a group, explore attitudes to personal space, especially the feelings that arise when someone's space is disregarded, intruded on or disturbed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, Blind Walks, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwManipulatingSpace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manipulating space"@en, "Raum handhaben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through examining and understanding how we perceive space, we are said to learn how to manipulate it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, Blind Walks, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGroupSpaceExplorationYieldsManipulatingSpace a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Group exploration of personal space yields handling of space"@en, "Gruppenerkundung des Raums führt zum Umgang mit Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Examining and understanding how we perceive space, here in a group, is said to teach how to manipulate it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGroupExplorationOfPersonalSpace ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwManipulatingSpace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
