pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoloSpaceObservationYieldsManipulatingSpace a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Solo observation in space yields handling of space"@en, "Selbstbeobachtung im Raum führt zum Umgang mit Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observing oneself in stillness and movement is the solo form of the same examination of space."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoloObservationInSpace ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwManipulatingSpace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, Blind Walks, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSoloObservationInSpace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Solo observation of oneself in space"@en, "Selbstbeobachtung im Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Observe yourself in a range of situations, both still and moving, noting your relationship with the surrounding space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, Blind Walks, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpaceAsMediumForRipples a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Space as a medium for sending ripples"@en, "Raum als Medium, um Wellen auszusenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling surrounding space as a medium or organ of communication through which ripples or waves can be sent out; T'ai Chi is recommended as a BodyMind exercise whose slow movements strengthen the sense of floating in a fluid-like medium."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBFlowingMeditation (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 practice imagines space as water and pushes and shapes it with the hands; here the capacity is feeling the surrounding space as a medium of communication along which ripples can be sent, with T'ai Chi named, not described, as a good exercise for it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Space Exercises, Blind Walks, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .



#
# Speech Exercises
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwVoiceAsCarrierOfPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The voice as carrier of power"@en, "Die Stimme als Kraftträger"@de ;
    skos:definition "The voice is held to be an important carrier of power; the term 'enchantment' is read as pointing to its old link with magic, and song, chant, invocation, prayer and even children's rhymes occur in all cultures as means of raising power, above all when joined with dance and music."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwFiveConditionsEffectiveSpeech a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five conditions for effective speech"@en, "Fünf Bedingungen wirksamen Sprechens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author lists what effective speaking needs: being self-assured; mindful of other people; at ease; clear-headed; and conscious of the effect one's words have on the situation (five numbered points)."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own numbered list (pm:Systematizing)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Walking Between the Worlds" ;
    dcterms:date "1986"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Use of the Voice, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwCarryingEmotionByVoice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Carrying emotion to others by voice"@en, "Gefühle durch die Stimme übertragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With practice and experience one can use the voice to convey emotions and feelings to others, from rousing them to enthusiasm and action to gently lulling them into relaxation with soft words and tones."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Use of the Voice, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGroupChants a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Group Chants"@en, "Gruppengesänge"@de ;
    skos:definition "A group chants a verse together, each member repeating the whole of it; examples range from a simple sun chant to the Wiccan 'Darksome Night and Shining Moon'. Whatever the content, a rhythm soon builds and carries everyone along."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Group Chants, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwRaisingPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Raising power"@en, "Kraft erheben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Raising power, for which group chanting is called one of the most effective means."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Group Chants, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGroupChantsYieldRaisingPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Group chants raise power"@en, "Gruppengesänge erheben Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group chanting is named among the most effective means of raising power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGroupChants ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwRaisingPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Group Chants, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwRhythmCarriesTheGroupSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rhythm carries the group"@en, "Rhythmus trägt die Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "In group chanting a rhythm is soon established that sweeps all participants along with it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of group chanting, a rhythm that soon builds up and carries everyone along, whatever the words express. No other mark of raised power is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Group Chants, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpinningMantra a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Spinning Mantra"@en, "Das kreisende Mantra"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of everyone chanting the whole verse, the lines are shared out, each person in turn voicing the next line, on a single note, stressing the same syllables in every line (e.g. the second and fourth). Variant: start seated in a circle, then each person in turn rises and wanders about, stopping before the others while keeping the chant going."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, The Spinning Mantra, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpinningMantraYieldsRaisingPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Spinning Mantra raises power"@en, "Das kreisende Mantra erhebt Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Spinning Mantra is given as a form of group chant, the means named for raising power."@en ;
    skos:note "The yield is carried over from the group chant, of which the text presents the Spinning Mantra as a form; no separate effect is named."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpinningMantra ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwRaisingPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, The Spinning Mantra, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGibberish a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Gibberish"@en, "Kauderwelsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "With a partner, pick a theme for a conversation and hold it without any recognisable words, trying to convey meaning purely by tone and inflection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Gibberish, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGibberishYieldsCarryingEmotion a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Gibberish trains expression through tone"@en, "Kauderwelsch schult den Ausdruck durch den Ton"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding a conversation without recognisable words aims at developing expression through tone and inflection alone."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwGibberish ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwCarryingEmotionByVoice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Gibberish, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwExploringTheVoiceOnTape a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exploring the voice with a tape recorder"@en, "Die Stimme mit dem Tonbandgerät erkunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explore the many ways the voice can be used, playing oneself back on a tape recorder for an instant replay, and begin with songs, chants and invocations that others have written."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Gibberish, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpontaneousInvocation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using words that come spontaneously"@en, "Spontan aufsteigende Worte gebrauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chant or invoke with words that arise in the moment instead of a text written by someone else."@en ;
    skos:note "Written as the later step named under Gibberish; the text gives no further procedure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Speech Exercises, Gibberish, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwConfidenceBeforeSpontaneousWordsPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Confidence before spontaneous invocation"@en, "Selbstvertrauen vor spontaner Anrufung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most people are said to begin with others' songs, chants and invocations and to move to spontaneous words only once their confidence has been built up; only sheer practice is said to achieve this."@en ;
    skos:note "An order of learning without a stated consequence of skipping it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwExploringTheVoiceOnTape ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwSpontaneousInvocation ;
