#
# Touch Exercises
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwTouchAsIntimateSense a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Touch as intimate sense"@en, "Tastsinn als intimer Sinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Touch (pressure, heat, texture) is taken for granted, yet vital to survival and especially intimate communication; joined with gentle words it can carry us into relaxation, sleep, visions or lovers' darkness. It is said often to become the leading sense in healing, inducing trance in others, and the psychic reading of things and locations; because loss of sight heightens tactile sensitivity, darkness or a blindfold is the suggested starting point."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Touch Exercises, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwHeightenedTactileSensitivity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heightened tactile sensitivity"@en, "Gesteigerte taktile Empfindsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enhanced awareness of touch, useful in healing, in sending others into trance and in psychically examining objects and places."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Touch Exercises, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwBlindExplorations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Blind Explorations"@en, "Blinde Erkundungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beginners' group exercise: partners sit opposite one another with eyes shut; one gently explores the other's hands with the fingers, letting impressions and images arise; if both are comfortable, faces may be explored too."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Touch Exercises, Blind Explorations, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

