pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwJourneyReturnToSurface a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Journey stage 7: Return to the surface"@en, "Reisestation 7: Rückkehr an die Oberfläche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The seventh stage: coming back up to the surface."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Going Down, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwJourneyReturnToCommunity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Journey stage 8: Return to the community"@en, "Reisestation 8: Rückkehr in die Gemeinschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The eighth stage: rejoining the community, in a role the text leaves open with a question mark."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Going Down, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwStrivingMatters a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The journey never ends; striving matters"@en, "Die Reise endet nie; das Streben zählt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The journey is called eternal and universal (the Fool, Luke Skywalker, everyone); the author disbelieves in utopias, perfection or blissful 'True Selves' and holds that the striving is what matters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), Going Down, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .



#
# closing remarks after Going Down
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwTechniquesOnlyABeginning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The techniques are only a beginning"@en, "Die Techniken sind nur ein Anfang"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author states the book's techniques are by no means definitive, merely a start, and that other works will help further."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), closing remarks after Going Down, p. 46; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsWbwExploringTechniquesWithFriends a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exploring the techniques with friends"@en, "Die Techniken mit Freunden erkunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recommended use of the book: find interested friends and explore the techniques together; no special trappings are needed, the BodyMind being enough at this stage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), closing remarks after Going Down, p. 46; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsWbwFasterLearningWithOthersSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faster learning with others"@en, "Schnelleres Lernen mit anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With others helping, one is told one will learn faster and enjoy it more."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of exploring the techniques with friends, faster learning and more fun; announced in advance, with no measure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:WalkingBetweenTheWorlds ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Walking Between the Worlds: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume One (Pagan News Publications, 1986; on-line version of December 1998), closing remarks after Going Down, p. 46; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 1_djvu.txt" .



#
# Volume 2: Two Worlds and Inbetween
#

#
# The Three Worlds
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiThreeWorlds a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Three Worlds as Hine's ordering of experience"@en, "Die Drei Welten als Hines Ordnung der Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine divides life experience into three interwoven arenas, the Social, the Mythic and the Personal, which are not separate realms but are pulled apart so that each can be examined and its share in the others seen, and he arranges the book's exercises under the three heads."@en ;
    skos:note "Merged with the pass-A record of the bare three-world schema, which states the same partition."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Two Worlds and Inbetween" ;
    dcterms:date "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, p. 5; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSocialWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Social World"@en, "Die soziale Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ordinary world of agreed, consensual reality, where shared conventions hold and people play roles under ground rules; its exercises work through group sharing and expression."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Social World, p. 5; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCompetenceManagingSocialWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Competence in managing the social world"@en, "Kompetenz im Umgang mit der sozialen Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Grasping the rules and games of social life is said to improve one's ability to cope in that world; weak awareness of its subtleties usually yields poor performances."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Social World, p. 5; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPoorGraspSocialSubtletiesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Poor grasp of social subtleties"@en, "Mangelndes Gespür für soziale Feinheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A poor understanding of the fine points of social conventions is said usually to result in poor performance in the social world."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of managing the social world, when the subtleties of its conventions are poorly grasped. No deadline; the rate word is usually; the cause is put on the operator's weak awareness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Social World, p. 5; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMythicWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Mythic World"@en, "Die mythische Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The realm of symbol and metaphor, of theatre, legend, fantasy and TV culture, where magick is most visible; here the shaman appears as a figure of myth mediating between personal vision and social cohesion, between spirits and the people."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCommunalEcstasyMediatingMyth (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node has the magician guide a community into its mythic world; here the Mythic World itself is defined, with the shaman as a mythic figure between personal vision and social cohesion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Mythic World, p. 5; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPersonalWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Personal World"@en, "Die persönliche Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The intimate, intrapsychic world of the self, the most mysterious of the three, whose depths are reached through the Mythic world; self-knowledge is held to be key to all magickal development."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 6; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWorkingWorldAloneInsufficientCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Working in one world alone is insufficient"@en, "Arbeit in nur einer Welt genügt nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns that development should be judged across all three worlds, not one only."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiThreeWorlds ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 6; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiChangeSeenInSocialWorldSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of development are sought in the social world"@en, "Zeichen der Entwicklung in der sozialen Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changes should be looked for in how one relates to and empathises with others; solitary workers should still note how the work alters their social feelings and behaviour and what changes others notice in them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of the whole work, to be read in the social world, in how one relates to and feels for others and what changes others see in one. Hine names where to look, not what counts, and nothing given separates change from its absence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 6; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiOthersSeeYouPratFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others see you as a prat"@en, "Andere halten einen für einen Trottel"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one's high self-regard is contradicted by everyone else's opinion, this is taken as a sign that something has gone wrong and needs reflection."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of the work as judged in the social world, when a high opinion of oneself meets everyone else's poor view. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator, who is told to consider where he is going wrong."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 6; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMythInbetween a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Myth as the inbetween"@en, "Der Mythos als das Dazwischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Mythic world stands between Social and Personal; myths draw on shared human experience, are rooted in the Deep Mind and give societies their driving rationale; in it social conventions can be overturned and psychic secrets voiced without disaster or loss of a stable self."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 6; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deep Mind"@en, "Der Tiefe Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "A layer of mind beyond personal awareness from which imagination and myths spring; elsewhere glossed as the subconscious; it throws up images matching the myths one has assimilated."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBDeepMindOceanSelfIceberg (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node pictures the Deep Mind as an ocean holding iceberg selves built of Personal, Social and Mythic structures; here it is the layer past personal awareness from which imagination and myth arise and which returns images fitting the myths one has absorbed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 6; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDestroyingPeoplesMythsBreaksWill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Destroying a people's myths breaks its will"@en, "Die Zerstörung der Mythen eines Volkes bricht seinen Willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Myths supply meaning and motive, from cultural fantasies of stardom or the presidency to that of becoming a shaman, and work on us so constantly that we barely notice them; hence tyrants learn that crushing a people's dreams and putting their own myths in place of its myths saps its will, and Hine counts the dream-worlds of Native Americans and Australian Aborigines as wrecked in this way by white invaders, who left them bound in a narrow, impoverished space."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 7; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMetaphorMistakenLiteralTruthCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Metaphor mistaken for literal truth"@en, "Metapher als wörtliche Wahrheit missverstanden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Myths are said to turn most hazardous and insidious once metaphor is read literally and stories harden into fixed dogma."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMythInbetween ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 7; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSelfChangeHealingEnteringMythicWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-change and healing by entering the Mythic world"@en, "Selbstwandlung und Heilung durch Eintritt in die mythische Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "By temporarily entering the Mythic world and enacting stories that lend experience mythic stature one is said to change oneself and thereby the world, reintegrate psychic contents, see oneself from new angles, outgrow conditioned habits and beliefs, and adopt new courses of action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 7; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMythicParticipationMayDisturbCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mythic participation may disturb"@en, "Mythische Teilhabe kann verstören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking part in the Mythic world can be shocking or disturbing, although above all it may heal."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSelfChangeHealingEnteringMythicWorld ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 7; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRenewedSenseExtraordinary a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Renewed sense of the extraordinary"@en, "Erneuertes Gespür für das Außergewöhnliche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Participation in mythic experience as actor, mediator or audience is said to restore a sense of life's dynamic vitality and of wonder inside everyday routine; myths intensify life passages such as birth, loss, death and renewal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 7; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiImaginationMediumMythic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imagination as the medium of the Mythic"@en, "Die Imagination als Medium des Mythischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagination, limited only by self-imposed barriers, is the medium of the Mythic; all ideas arise in it and it rises out of the Deep Mind, which lies past personal awareness and the social world; tension exists between paramount social reality and individual dreams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 7; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMagickOrganisationImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick as an organisation of the imagination"@en, "Magie als Organisation der Imagination"@de ;
    skos:definition "A modern definition cited by the author: exploring the Personal and its interplay with the Social through a set of mythic symbols produces experiences meaningful within those myths; assimilating ideas until familiar shapes the imagination so that the Deep Mind returns matching images."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAOrganisationOfImagination (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node ties the definition to rituals needing a prepared, coherent frame; here it is tied to exploring the Personal and Social through a set of mythic symbols, whose assimilation makes the Deep Mind answer in kind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 8; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPluralMythicMapsScouts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plural mythic maps and scouts"@en, "Vielfalt mythischer Landkarten und Kundschafter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering the Deep Mind needs signposts and maps supplied by visionaries, artists, shamans and magicians, though anyone may act as a scout; modern culture offers many mythic maps that one may adopt in turn, each time holding the current one to be truer than the rest; an unrestrained imagination turns longings into aims and achievable reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 8; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMythicPowerOfFiction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fiction has mythic power; historical validity irrelevant"@en, "Fiktion hat mythische Kraft; historische Gültigkeit unerheblich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within the Mythic world historical truth does not matter; a story that moves us and gives a valid, powerful experience reconnecting us to deep aspects of ourselves serves its purpose; the many mythic pools of cultures and fiction are both an advantage and a problem."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCIntensityOfBelief (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node says any system, historical or fictional, works by intensity of belief; here historical validity is said to drop out once one is inside the Mythic world, and the many mythic and fictional pools are called both gain and difficulty."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 8; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAgainstCriticsLynnAndrewsCarlosCastaneda a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against critics of Lynn Andrews and Carlos Castaneda"@en, "Gegen die Kritiker von Lynn Andrews und Carlos Castaneda"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author notes that Andrews and Castaneda are attacked for writing fiction posing as fact, and replies that regardless their works made shamanic techniques accessible and serve as an entry point to uncharted realms."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read; the critics are not named, so the dispute stands as his claim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 9; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShamanismEssenceRatherThanMethod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanism as an essence rather than a method"@en, "Schamanismus als Wesen statt Methode"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the author shamanism is less a set way of doing things than a thread running through all his magick; the bones, not the flesh, matter; it satisfies him and his clients and colleagues and he aspires to nothing greater with it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), The Three Worlds, The Personal World, p. 9; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .




#
# Exploring Our Personal Worlds
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAimPersonalWorldExercises a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Aim of the Personal World exercises"@en, "Ziel der Übungen zur persönlichen Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "These exercises turn awareness towards the inner dynamics forming self-image, the half-heard internal dialogues from which our story of self grows; written for solo work, adaptable for groups or discussion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerConversationsStories a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner conversations and stories"@en, "Innere Gespräche und Geschichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Behaviour, beliefs and attitudes are shaped by stories we tell ourselves, often of the form that one cannot do something because of something; many stem from early learning or intense emotion, some are repressed, and they act as self-fulfilling prophecies limiting one's possibilities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExaminingRevisingInnerConversations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Examining and revising inner conversations"@en, "Innere Gespräche prüfen und umschreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify the limiting inner conversations (including ones hidden behind a vague sense that something is going wrong), become aware of one's faults, weaknesses and blind spots, then revise or challenge the conversations and act against them, approaching such problems one at a time rather than all at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSelfAwarenessBeforeEffectiveSelfDevelopmentPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-awareness before effective self-development"@en, "Selbstwahrnehmung vor wirksamer Selbstentwicklung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing one's own failings, weak points and blind spots is called essential for developing oneself to act more effectively; no consequence of skipping is stated."@en ;
    skos:note "Called essential, but no consequence of leaving it out is given."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExaminingRevisingInnerConversations ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBreakingSelfImposedLimits ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInitiationBringsUnpleasantSelfRealisationCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation brings unpleasant self-realisation"@en, "Initiation bringt unangenehme Selbsterkenntnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "A period of initiation may force the recognition that one has behaved foolishly for months; such moments are always unpleasant, yet one should then act on them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExaminingRevisingInnerConversations ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDeeplyEmbeddedOrInvestedConversationsResistFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deeply embedded or invested conversations resist change"@en, "Tief verankerte Gespräche widerstehen der Veränderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The deeper a conversation is lodged, the more it resists change, often because one has a stake in keeping it, e.g. it makes giving up easy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of revising inner conversations, which resist change the more deeply they are lodged, often because one has a stake in keeping them. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the operator's investment in the old story."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBreakingSelfImposedLimits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking self-imposed limits"@en, "Selbstauferlegte Grenzen durchbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Escaping limits one has set oneself is likened to entering a new world where one can do what seemed impossible; the author means mundane things such as getting on with parents, clearing an overdraft or keeping a job, not flying or world mastery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRevisingConversationsYieldsFreedomSelfLimits a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Revising conversations yields freedom from self-limits"@en, "Umschreiben der Gespräche führt zur Befreiung von Selbstbegrenzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Challenging and revising inner conversations is presented as the route to breaking self-imposed limits."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExaminingRevisingInnerConversations ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBreakingSelfImposedLimits ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiProblemsOneAtATimeCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Problems cannot be tackled all at once"@en, "Probleme lassen sich nicht alle auf einmal angehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Such life problems can be approached only if one is aware of them and ready to act, and not simultaneously."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExaminingRevisingInnerConversations ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWarriorsFoesLieOrdinaryWorlds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The warrior's foes lie in the ordinary worlds"@en, "Die Feinde des Kriegers liegen in den gewöhnlichen Welten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Would-be impeccable warriors meet their worst enemies in the Social and Personal worlds, not the Mythic; these enemies are self-built barriers clung to with growing tension."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Stories & Conversations, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShields a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shields"@en, "Schilde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make a symbolic representation of oneself and what matters most (ideals, directions one wants to travel), as simple or elaborate as wished: free-form painting, collage, a four-quartered wheel with oneself in the middle, or a mandala; use it in group sharing discussions of personal feelings and ideals."@en ;
    skos:note "Source attributes the exercise to The Shamanic Development Course; found in many forms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Shields, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShieldMapOnesFieldExperience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shield as map of one's field of experience"@en, "Schild als Landkarte des eigenen Erfahrungsfeldes"@de ;
    skos:definition "A shield is said to serve as a map of one's own field of experience, showing its territories, peaks of interest, hopes and fears, useful for sharing with others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Shields, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShieldsYieldMapSelf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Shields yield a map of the self"@en, "Schilde ergeben eine Selbstkarte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making a shield produces a symbolic map of one's experience."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShields ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShieldMapOnesFieldExperience ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
