pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiYearWheels a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Year Wheels"@en, "Jahresräder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Groups that hold seasonal rites may build a Year Wheel showing symbols, images and talisman-like objects taken from every rite of the year, reflecting and reminding members of how the group grew over the year."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Shields, p. 12; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiImagesAriseLikeDaydreamVisionsSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Images arise like daydream visions"@en, "Bilder steigen wie Tagtraumvisionen auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "The working state of scrying is signalled by images arising in the mind much like daydreams or the pictures seen before falling asleep."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of scrying, pictures rising like daydreams or the images before sleep. It marks the state reached, not the truth of what is seen."@en, "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBScrying (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice gives the daydream-like images as part of the instruction; here they are read as the mark that the light trance of scrying has been reached."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Scrying, p. 12; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRelaxationOrCenteringBeforeScryingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxation or Centering before scrying"@en, "Entspannung oder Zentrierung vor dem Scrying"@de ;
    skos:definition "A meditation or relaxation exercise beforehand is suggested, and a Centering ritual before and after scrying is recommended."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBScrying (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice names a meditation or relaxation before scrying; here a Centering rite before and after the session is recommended as well."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringExerciseGeneralForm ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondBScrying ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Scrying, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPathworkingsAidScrying a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pathworkings as an aid to scrying"@en, "Pfadarbeiten als Hilfe zum Scrying"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pathworkings designed to relax and to stimulate the Deep (subconscious) Mind into producing images may be used in support of scrying."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBUsesPathworking (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node lets a pathworking leave open spaces in which to scry; here pathworkings that relax and stir the Deep Mind are offered as an aid to scrying."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Scrying, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiScryingCausesDrowsinessCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Scrying causes drowsiness"@en, "Scrying macht schläfrig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Scrying can make one drowsy, so initial practice sessions should not run long."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicCondBScrying ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Scrying, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSmokeMirror a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Smoke Mirror"@en, "Rauchspiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit or lie down after Centering, or after some minutes of relaxing with deep breaths, and grow quiet; picture each outgoing breath turning to smoke that gathers into a cloud and clears into a full-length mirror; study the reflection calmly, noting posture and any part of the body it enlarges; as it clouds over, recall yourself at some age under twelve and let that figure form, asking how you looked and dressed, who your friends were, what angered or frightened you and what you wished changed; let the mirror open as a door to the past and talk back and forth with the younger self; then let it cloud into smoke again, breathe it in while keeping the memory of the meeting, and count down from ten to waking. For full effect the script is put on cassette, the waking call is followed by soft bell tones, and any insights are set down on paper or tape; it also serves groups."@en ;
    skos:note "Called by Hine a guided fantasy rather than a pathworking, adapted from a dramatherapy exercise first devised by Marsha Robbins. Written by the integrator from the reconcile step: the pass-A record of this practice carried only that attribution and no steps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Smoke Mirror, pp. 13-14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringOrRelaxationBeforeSmokeMirrorPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering or relaxation before the Smoke Mirror"@en, "Zentrierung oder Entspannung vor dem Rauchspiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise is to be preceded by Centering or by some minutes of relaxing and breathing deeply."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringExerciseGeneralForm ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSmokeMirror ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Smoke Mirror, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTherapeuticRecoveryMemorySelfAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Therapeutic recovery of memory and self-awareness"@en, "Therapeutische Erinnerung und Selbstwahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meeting one's younger selves is said to be therapeutic, helping memory and self-awareness and reminding us how much of the adult self grew from earlier experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Smoke Mirror, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSmokeMirrorYieldsMemorySelfAwareness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Smoke Mirror yields memory and self-awareness"@en, "Rauchspiegel fördert Erinnerung und Selbstwahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meeting one's younger self in the Smoke Mirror is said to aid memory and self-awareness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSmokeMirror ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTherapeuticRecoveryMemorySelfAwareness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Smoke Mirror, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAgainstOverlyPsychologicalInwardOnlyApproachCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against an overly psychological, inward-only approach"@en, "Gegen eine allzu psychologische, nur nach innen gerichtete Haltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting shamanic practice in a modern context easily slides into excessive psychologising and inner-directedness; one should remember that power is also all around us, in cosmic tides and in Power Spots."@en ;
    skos:note "Section developed from ideas of Stephen Mace."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPowerSpots ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPowerSpots a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power Spots"@en, "Kraftorte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Power Spots may be regarded as magickal vents in the earth's surface, openings in Gaia's skin; once located and made knowable they may be drawn upon; discovery is personal and calls for intuition, critical judgement and good sense, the Personal World here arising from one's interaction with the landscape."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine says the section grew from the ideas of the American magician Stephen Mace."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGaiaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Gaia"@en, "Gaia"@de ;
    skos:definition "The earth figured as a living being whose skin has pores, namely the Power Spots."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPsnGaiaNaming (The Pseudonomicon, 1994): the 1994 node names Gaia as a vast non-human presence met in a working; here Gaia is the living earth whose skin has pores, the Power Spots."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Gaia" ;
    pm:nameRole "the earth as a living body" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTappingPowerSpot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tapping a Power Spot"@en, "Einen Kraftort anzapfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A found Power Spot is said to be able to supplement one's own power, or to offer contact points into the innerworlds, giving access to and knowledge of other entities sharing the biosphere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPlaceCanDrainPowerCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A place can drain power"@en, "Ein Ort kann Kraft absaugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing Castaneda and Lynn Andrews: just as power may pour from a place, a place may also suck power into itself to the harm of the unwary."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine reports this warning from Carlos Castaneda and Lynn Andrews; their works are not read through him."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTappingPowerSpot ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiNotEveryStoneCircleSuitsRitualCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not every stone circle or ley point suits ritual"@en, "Nicht jeder Steinkreis oder Leypunkt eignet sich für Rituale"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is a common but mistaken belief that every stone circle and ley point is a fit place for ritual or magickal work."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPowerSpots ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSensingVibesPlace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing the vibes of a place"@en, "Die Schwingung eines Ortes erspüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before working at a place, assess its atmosphere by making oneself receptive to fleeting impressions (as in Walking Between the Worlds), or by dowsing or scrying."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCrossroadsTraditionalPowerSpots a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crossroads as traditional power spots"@en, "Kreuzungen als traditionelle Kraftorte"@de ;
    skos:definition "The place where roads cross is a traditional power spot associated with several deities and with folk tales of meeting the devil; the author jokingly extends this to motorway tangles such as Spaghetti Junction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiHecateNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Hecate"@en, "Hekate"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hecate is named as a deity linked with the crossroads as a traditional power spot (Greek)."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Hecate" ;
    pm:nameRole "Greek deity associated with crossroads" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
