pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPapaLegbaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Papa Legba"@en, "Papa Legba"@de ;
    skos:definition "Papa Legba is named as a deity linked with the crossroads as a traditional power spot (Haitian)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBLegbaNaming (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node is the god who possessed some three hundred marchers at once; here Papa Legba is named as a deity of the crossroads as a traditional power spot."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Papa Legba" ;
    pm:nameRole "Haitian deity associated with crossroads" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDevilAtCrossroadsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The devil at the crossroads"@en, "Der Teufel an der Kreuzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Folk tales tell of meeting the devil where roads cross."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the devil" ;
    pm:nameRole "folkloric figure met at crossroads" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTwoTypesPowerSpot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two types of Power Spot"@en, "Zwei Arten von Kraftorten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first type is tied to a specific kind of power, a place of contact where one can trance and project into a fitting innerworld to feel an element; the second type is harder to find and depends on openness to clairvoyance, signs and sense awareness, recognisable by incongruities of terrain."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalAttunementAtPowerSpot a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental attunement at a Power Spot"@en, "Elementare Einstimmung an einem Kraftort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go to a place matching the desired power (a cave or narrow valley for earth, a lookout where the tide surges round for the sea, the roof of a tall building for a city), enter trance (methods in WBTW) and project oneself into an appropriate innerworld to gain understanding or a feeling of that element."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTranceBeforePowerSpotProjectionPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Trance techniques from WBTW before power-spot projection"@en, "Trancetechniken aus WBTW vor der Projektion am Kraftort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering trance, as taught in Walking Between the Worlds, precedes projecting into an innerworld at a power spot."@en ;
    skos:note "For the trance techniques the text points to Walking Between the Worlds; the existing node for entering trance at will stands for them here."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicCondBEnteringProlongingTranceWill ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalAttunementAtPowerSpot ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRapportElementOrPlacePower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rapport with an element or place-power"@en, "Verbindung zu einem Element oder einer Ortskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "One can gain understanding of, or feeling for, a specific element and enhance rapport with earth, sea or the brooding urban energies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPowerSpotTranceYieldsElementalRapport a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Power-spot trance yields elemental rapport"@en, "Trance am Kraftort führt zu elementarer Verbindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering trance at a place suited to an element and projecting into a fitting innerworld is said to give a feel for that element."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalAttunementAtPowerSpot ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRapportElementOrPlacePower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFindingPowerSpotsIncongruitiesTerrain a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding Power Spots by incongruities of terrain"@en, "Kraftorte an Unstimmigkeiten des Geländes erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Look for features that contrast starkly with the surroundings, such as a lone rock amid broad grassland or marsh, or a single spring or tree on a mountainside; then discover by personal experiment which activity the spot suits (trance work, centering)."@en ;
    skos:note "Text says this is the easiest means of spotting the \"more specific type\", wording that seems to conflict with the preceding sentence on the second type."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWeirdNotAutomaticallyUsableMalignSpotsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Weird is not automatically usable; malign spots"@en, "Seltsam heißt nicht brauchbar; bösartige Orte"@de ;
    skos:definition "A spot feeling strange does not make it good to use; some feel definitely malign and should be left alone, though not necessarily evil; all powerful places deserve respect and we have no automatic right to use any place."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicPsnApproachingPlaceOfPower (The Pseudonomicon, 1994): the 1994 practice says how to approach a place of power with respect; here the point is that strangeness does not license use, that some spots are malign and best left alone, and that no one has an automatic right to a place."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFindingPowerSpotsIncongruitiesTerrain ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGeniusLociNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Genius Loci"@en, "Genius Loci"@de ;
    skos:definition "A place spirit: the lore that particular spots are guarded by their own guardians; one should bear it in mind when approaching power spots."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPsnGeniusLociGestalt (The Pseudonomicon, 1994): the 1994 node reads the spirit of a place as the gestalt of its ecology, history and the visitor's awareness; here it is the folk lore that particular spots have guardians, to be kept in mind when approaching power spots."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Genius Loci" ;
    pm:nameRole "guardian spirit of a place" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBeingLedOmens a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Being led by omens"@en, "Sich von Omen leiten lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Go out, through fields or city streets, willing to let omens lead the way, such as animal encounters, unusual clouds or chance meetings with friends, staying open to adventure and behaving as though such signs are real."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInterestingResultsOmenLedWanderingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Interesting results from omen-led wandering"@en, "Interessante Ergebnisse beim omengeleiteten Umherstreifen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who go out prepared to follow omens are told they will often get interesting results."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of wandering led by omens, which often brings interesting results. The rate word is often; what counts as interesting is left open."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCatLeadsAuthorPowerSpotOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cat leads the author to a power spot"@en, "Von einer Katze zu einem Kraftort geführt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author reports a cat insisting he follow it over fields to a tree stump that was a power spot, after which it ran off."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: Hine was led by a cat over fields to a stump he took for a power spot. A single case; that the stump was a power spot rests on his judgement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiHeightenedAwarenessSurroundingsTheirPulse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heightened awareness of surroundings and their pulse"@en, "Gesteigerte Wahrnehmung der Umgebung und ihres Pulses"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mindful wandering is said to enhance physical and psychic awareness of surroundings and one's relation to the landscapes passed through, letting one sense each place's pulse and the subtle changing patterns of life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiOmenLedWanderingYieldsAwarenessSurroundings a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Omen-led wandering yields awareness of surroundings"@en, "Omengeleitetes Umherstreifen fördert Umgebungswahrnehmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wandering open to omens is said to sharpen physical and psychic awareness of one's surroundings."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBeingLedOmens ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiHeightenedAwarenessSurroundingsTheirPulse ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGardenOfPersonOfPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The person of power's garden"@en, "Der Garten des Menschen der Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Haitian shamans are reported to say each person of power has a garden, which may extend no further than the front gate or across a city region; feeling the ripples in it, via dream or vision, when changes happen and visitors arrive, is called essential to magickal living."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine reports the saying from Haitian shamans."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFindingYourPlacePower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding your Place of Power"@en, "Den eigenen Kraftplatz finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chalk a circle nine feet across in a room; members walk round it trying to feel the most fitting place for them and sit there once decided; when all have chosen, a compass is brought and the four directions identified; then use this to open a discussion on what the circle and the cardinal directions mean in magick."@en ;
    skos:note "Developed by Sheila Broun for the Shamanic Development Course; Hine reports doing it with a group."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Personal Worlds, Power Spots, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .




#
# Exploring Our Social Worlds
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCommunalStrengthGroupShamanicWork a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The communal strength of group shamanic work"@en, "Die gemeinschaftliche Stärke schamanischer Gruppenarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A main strength of group work is the communal sense: in a space of mutual inspiration simple exercises bring striking results, showing little need for book knowledge or teachers; shamanic magick is grounded in the social life of meetings and gatherings, and all inner work must eventually return to the surrounding world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSoundscapes a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Soundscapes"@en, "Klanglandschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group members brainstorm around a chosen theme, each picks a word or phrase as the seed of a chant and develops an individual rhythm, pitch and tempo; the layered voices build a sound picture conveying the theme's atmosphere (example: a drama group voicing advertising jingles for the theme of sweets)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Soundscapes, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiEvokingMoodsGroupGrownChants a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evoking moods and group-grown chants"@en, "Stimmungen hervorrufen und gruppengewachsene Gesänge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Soundscapes can be used to call up and heighten moods, and to develop chants grown by the group for ritual and spellcasting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Soundscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSoundscapesYieldMoodEvocationChants a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Soundscapes yield mood evocation and chants"@en, "Klanglandschaften ergeben Stimmungen und Gesänge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group soundscapes are said to call up and heighten moods and to grow chants for ritual and spellcasting."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSoundscapes ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiEvokingMoodsGroupGrownChants ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Soundscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGroupGestaltMindSharedDreams a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group Gestalt mind and shared dreams"@en, "Gestalt-Geist der Gruppe und geteilte Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "As a group forms, members grow intimate and this may show as shared dreams or dreams about the group; the group develops a common psychic space, called the Gestalt mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBSharedDreamsTheirValidation (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node defines a shared dream and says only telling the others validates it; here shared dreams mark a forming group, which grows a common psychic space called its Gestalt mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDreamscaping a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreamscaping"@en, "Traumszenen-Spiel (Dreamscaping)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A role-play development: one person tells a dream; the group turns its elements into a dramatic event in which the dreamer plays one of the dream figures and someone else takes the dreamer's role; themes may be chosen (e.g. members share recurring nightmares and script a play from everyone's imagery), built up with soundscaping, tapes, lighting, masks and props."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine met the method in The Theatre of Voodoo, an experimental drama group."@en, "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicPrcCDreamscaping (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 practice is a solitary Mythos technique of meditated image sequences followed into sleep; here dreamscaping is a group drama in which a member's dream is staged and the dreamer plays one of its figures."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGroupMythicWorldReachedThroughDreamsOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A group mythic world reached through dreams"@en, "Eine mythische Gruppenwelt, erreichbar durch Träume"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working with one another's dream images developed a sort of shared mythic world for the group that could be accessed via dreams and group activities, and images from members' dream-worlds began to bleed into each other's dreams."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: in The Theatre of Voodoo, work with one another's dream images grew a group mythic world reachable through dreams and group activity, and images began to cross between members' dreams. A group report without counts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUnderstandingOnesOwnDreamSymbolism a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding one's own dream symbolism"@en, "Verständnis der eigenen Traumsymbolik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting out dreams is said to benefit understanding of one's own dream symbolism."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDreamscapingYieldsDreamUnderstanding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dreamscaping yields dream understanding"@en, "Dreamscaping fördert Traumverständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Staging dreams as group drama is said to help one understand one's own dream symbols."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDreamscaping ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUnderstandingOnesOwnDreamSymbolism ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDreamscapingCanTriggerEmotionalSurgesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Dreamscaping can trigger emotional surges"@en, "Dreamscaping kann emotionale Wellen auslösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dreamscaping may release emotional surges and should be approached carefully."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDreamscaping ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDreamsSocialWorldInterpenetrate a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dreams and the social world interpenetrate"@en, "Träume und soziale Welt durchdringen einander"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though thought highly personal, dreams can be carried over into social life, and the social world can offer a back door into them; the author wonders whether a sleeping person's dreamworld could be entered this way."@en ;
    skos:note "The entry into another's dream is raised only as an open question, not claimed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Dreamscapes, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMimingMessages a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Miming messages"@en, "Botschaften pantomimisch vermitteln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to convey messages by mime is called a useful skill belonging to the shamanic repertoire of tricksters, sacred clowns and performers, used also in healing or wrestling with spirits."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMimeHealingExtractingSpirit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mime in healing: extracting a spirit"@en, "Pantomime in der Heilung: Herausziehen eines Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "A described scene of a woman miming the pulling of a resisting wormlike thing from a seated man's ear may be comedy or a shamanka curing a client by drawing out a harmful spirit; mime is thus part of magick such as healing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPhysicalLanguageSpeaksDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical language speaks to the Deep Mind"@en, "Körpersprache spricht zum Tiefen Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spoken language mostly addresses waking awareness while physical languages address the Deep Mind directly; gestures draw power from our near-automatic reactions, convey messages faster than words and reinforce the power of a spoken phrase; this leads to sacred gestures of dancers, bodymind disciplines and ritual."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBRitualTheatreArtaudsPhysicalLanguage (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node takes the physical language of theatre from Artaud; here the claim is Hine's own, that gesture bypasses waking awareness and speaks to the Deep Mind, which is why mime belongs to magick."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiConflictingWordGestureDemonstration a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Conflicting word and gesture demonstration"@en, "Demonstration widersprüchlicher Worte und Gesten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Have people give a spoken message while gesturing the opposite, e.g. saying come here while signalling stay or go away, to show the power of gesture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiStudyingSignLanguages a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying sign languages"@en, "Gebärdensprachen studieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Study sign languages, for instance those for people without speech or those used where silence is vital in hunting or war, as a route to understanding sacred gesture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShapeShiftingByMimingAnyFigure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shape-shifting through mime of any recognisable figure"@en, "Gestaltwandel durch Pantomime beliebiger erkennbarer Figuren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beyond shape-shifting (from WBTW), any recognisable character, folkloric or from TV soaps, may be mimed if it has a base characteristic to work on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementals a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elementals"@en, "Elementarwesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The group lies down well spaced while the facilitator, seated on a stool at the centre, announces in the role of a great wizard that they will be allowed to take on elemental natures; the wizard calls out evocative image-phrases in turn (earth: shifting plates, grinding granite, volcanoes; fire: dancing, consuming flames; air: breezes, gusts, tornadoes; water: depths, currents, breakers turning to rock) and the group mimes the feelings evoked; end by returning to earth and rest, or go on into the growth of trees or cities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Elementals, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalsRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elementals in ritual"@en, "Elementarwesen im Ritual"@de ;
    skos:definition "During rituals, people act as elementals, dancing or miming their element; this is enhanced if each person explores their own relationship with each element."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Elementals, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAddingElementsPowerRitual a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Adding an element's power to a ritual"@en, "Die Kraft eines Elements dem Ritual hinzufügen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dancing or miming an element in ritual is said to add that element's power to the rite."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Elementals, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalMimeRitualAddsElementalPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental mime in ritual adds elemental power"@en, "Elementare Pantomime im Ritual verleiht Elementkraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elementals dancing or miming their element in a rite are said to lend the rite that element's power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalsRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAddingElementsPowerRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Elementals, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMimeGames a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mime Games"@en, "Pantomimespiele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group games: sit in a circle and mime an action to the person beside you, who guesses it; mime each other's typical postures and gestures; perform two-minute playlets such as quick mimes of creation myths; act mimes in slow motion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime Games, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSlowMotionMimeGroupTrance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced group trance via slow-motion mime"@en, "Vertiefte Gruppentrance durch Zeitlupen-Pantomime"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slow-motion mime combined with other techniques is said to be very effective in deepening group trances; the games also introduce the power of gesture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Social Worlds, Mime Games, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMimeGamesYieldGroupTranceEnhancement a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mime games yield group trance enhancement"@en, "Pantomimespiele vertiefen Gruppentrance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Slow-motion mime, joined with other techniques, is said to deepen group trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMimeGames ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSlowMotionMimeGroupTrance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
