#
# Exploring Our Mythic Worlds
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldsMindscapes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworlds as mindscapes"@en, "Innenwelten als Geisteslandschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "The innerworlds are mindscapes one travels in, meeting entities and undergoing transformative learning through stories and cycles of mythic proportion; calling them simply real or merely imaginary both misunderstand imagination, and in magick the subjective/objective distinction becomes obsolete."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiChangeThroughStructuredImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Change through structured imagination"@en, "Wandlung durch strukturierte Imagination"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagination given structure by symbolic images is said to release Deep Mind energies to change ourselves (identity work), influence our bodymind complexes, or bring about changes in external reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldsRealFarBeliefInvested a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworlds are real as far as belief is invested"@en, "Innenwelten sind so wirklich wie der investierte Glaube"@de ;
    skos:definition "Innerworlds are real insofar as belief is invested; they reflect and reinforce specific transformative learning, allowing awareness to be focused on one set of experiences, isolated and intensified out of what Spare termed the normal chaos."@en ;
    skos:note "The phrase for the normal chaos is ascribed by Hine to Austin Osman Spare."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 23; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInitiationTriggeredFilmOrTelevision a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation triggered by film or television"@en, "Durch Film oder Fernsehen ausgelöste Initiation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Periods of initiation are said sometimes to be set off by a film or TV programme."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBeliefMakesInnerworldsMythicFilmTV a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief makes innerworlds mythic; film and TV as innerworlds"@en, "Glaube macht Innenwelten mythisch; Film und Fernsehen als Innenwelten"@de ;
    skos:definition "We relate to innerworlds as to film or TV worlds: known to be illusory yet gripping; belief makes them real, and many people investing belief in an innerworld over time lend it power until it becomes mythic, reflecting our psychology through stereotyped entities; electronic and magickal innerworlds differ chiefly in intensity of transformative experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiLughNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Lugh"@en, "Lugh"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cited as a figure of the old mystery religions/myth less widely known than Mr Spock."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Lugh" ;
    pm:nameRole "mythic figure (Celtic), contrasted with Spock" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSpockNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Spock"@en, "Spock"@de ;
    skos:definition "Star Trek character read as a mythic stereotype who embodies logic."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCSpockNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node makes Spock the figure to invoke for dealing with computers; here Spock is one of the Star Trek characters read as a mythic stereotype, the embodiment of logic."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Spock" ;
    pm:nameRole "mythic stereotype in Star Trek" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSenseDiscrimination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sense of discrimination"@en, "Unterscheidungsvermögen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sooner or later one must develop discrimination about what serves oneself amid the many experts and authorities of magick and shamanism; pathworkings are said to help develop it along with intuition."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcADiscrimination (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node defines discrimination as finding what suits oneself by one's own research; here it is the faculty the crowd of experts forces one to grow, and which pathworking helps develop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUsingFictionalUniverseMythicWorldChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using a fictional universe as a mythic world for change"@en, "Ein fiktionales Universum als mythische Welt zur Wandlung nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With some modification, a fictional universe such as Star Trek may be entered as a Mythic world to bring about change; the author says he could use it so."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRolePlayYieldsMythicParticipationChange a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Role-play yields mythic participation for change"@en, "Rollenspiel ermöglicht mythische Teilhabe zur Wandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Group role-play of a fictional universe is said to make it usable, with some changes, as a mythic world for change."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicCondCRolePlayingMythos ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUsingFictionalUniverseMythicWorldChange ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiNoInnerworldCyclePrivileged a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No innerworld cycle is privileged; age is not power"@en, "Kein Mythenzyklus ist bevorzugt; Alter ist nicht Macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author favours no set of innerworlds (Star Trek, Celtic myth, the Tarot trumps, alchemy, Greek creation tales, Amerind worlds); against the view that older cycles are more powerful, clarity of the cycle's essential nature in its images matters more, since old myths have often been tampered with and bent by politics."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiOlderMythsNotMorePowerful a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the claim that older myths are more powerful"@en, "Gegen die Behauptung, ältere Mythen seien mächtiger"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some hold that a mythic cycle gains power with age; the author rejects this as not necessarily true."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read; the opponents are not named."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcCAgainstClaimFictionalGodsLess (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node rejects the claim that fictional entities are less valid than historical deities; here the rejected claim is that a mythic cycle grows in power with age, answered by the clarity of a cycle's nature and the political bending of old myths."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUnderlyingStructureOverSurfaceDetail a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Underlying structure over surface detail"@en, "Zugrunde liegende Struktur vor Oberflächendetail"@de ;
    skos:definition "In approaching innerworlds the underlying structure matters, not surface details; six guidelines follow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSixInnerworldGuidelines a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Six guidelines for innerworlds"@en, "Sechs Leitlinien für Innenwelten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's numbered six points for approaching innerworlds: consistency, sparse detail, challenging situations, using a map, not overdoing it, keeping records."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine's own numbered points, not stages of a procedure."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Two Worlds and Inbetween" ;
    dcterms:date "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldConsistentSymbolism a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Guideline 1: internal consistency of symbolism"@en, "Leitlinie 1: innere Stimmigkeit der Symbolik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep the symbolism and imagery of an innerworld internally consistent, e.g. no laser gun in a Celtic world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInconsistentIntrusionsWeakenBeliefFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inconsistent intrusions weaken belief"@en, "Unstimmige Einbrüche schwächen den Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "An obviously out-of-place element undermines belief in the innerworld's realness."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of belief in an innerworld, when something plainly foreign intrudes on its symbolism. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the design of the working."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldSparseDetail a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Guideline 2: do not over-detail"@en, "Leitlinie 2: nicht zu detailliert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not overload an innerworld with detail; leave free areas for the imagination where symbols grow organically out of the Deep Mind; the simplest symbols, clearly stated or briefly glimpsed, are often the most powerful."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiOverDetailedInnerworldFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Over-detailed innerworld"@en, "Überdetaillierte Innenwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "An innerworld made too detailed takes hours to work through and leaves no room for imagination to flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of an innerworld built in so much detail that it takes hours and leaves the imagination no free room. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the design of the working."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPathworkingSetMoodScryingDesertJackal a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pathworking to set the mood for scrying (desert and jackal guide)"@en, "Pfadarbeit zur Einstimmung auf das Scrying (Wüste und Schakalführer)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A simple guided walk through a desert to two vast rock pillars, between which a jackal-headed god, described only as opener of the way, leads the participants into an underground temple where the scrying then takes place."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAnubisNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Anubis"@en, "Anubis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The jackal-headed Egyptian god, here a guide and opener of the way who leads into an underground temple in a pathworking."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Anubis" ;
    pm:nameRole "guide, opener of the way" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPersonalUntraditionalImageAnubisOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Personal, untraditional image of Anubis"@en, "Persönliches, untraditionelles Bild des Anubis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author saw the loosely described guide as a jackal-headed humanoid in complex body-armour with pipes, circuitry and laser beams; not traditional but fitting for him, which is what counts."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report: in a loosely described pathworking Hine saw the jackal-headed guide as an armoured humanoid hung with pipes and circuits, untraditional but right for him. A single case; the measure is personal fit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldChallengingSituations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Guideline 3: enter challenging situations"@en, "Leitlinie 3: herausfordernde Situationen betreten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A pleasant innerworld suffices if relaxation is the aim; for change such as identity work, enter challenging, daunting and even frightening situations, focusing on various facets of oneself mirrored in mythic images."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTriggeringTransformativeProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Triggering the transformative process"@en, "Den Wandlungsprozess auslösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "An innerworld working focusing on aspects of the self is said to trigger the transformative process enabling adaptation and desired change; many journeys are mock deaths that threaten ego breakdown so that one transforms into more vital patterns; more potent images reach further into the Deep Mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiChallengingInnerworldWorkYieldsTransformation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Challenging innerworld work yields transformation"@en, "Herausfordernde Innenweltarbeit bewirkt Wandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entering daunting innerworld situations is said to set off the transformative process."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldChallengingSituations ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTriggeringTransformativeProcess ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldUseOfMap a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Guideline 4: use a map"@en, "Leitlinie 4: eine Landkarte benutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use a cosmological or psychological map (from fictional worlds to shamanic cosmologies to Qabalah) to find one's way into, around and out of an innerworld; learn the well-trodden paths before risking invisible routes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMapsCircuitDiagrams a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Maps as circuit diagrams"@en, "Landkarten als Schaltpläne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Maps are not arbitrary but channel and steer the energies reached in symbolic structures; like circuit diagrams they differentiate aspects of experience, and ordered patterns of experience let us harness the Deep Mind, entering different mythic structures for particular goals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDiscoveringSecretRoutesUnmappedTerritories a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Discovering secret routes and unmapped territories"@en, "Geheime Wege und unkartierte Gebiete entdecken"@de ;
    skos:definition "With development one is said to find secret routes to unmarked territories or entirely unmapped ones; sacred maps have hidden doors entered only by those knowing the sacred alignments."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWellTroddenPathsBeforeInvisibleRoutesPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Well-trodden paths before invisible routes"@en, "Ausgetretene Pfade vor unsichtbaren Wegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must know one's way around the familiar paths before taking chances with hidden routes."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldUseOfMap ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDiscoveringSecretRoutesUnmappedTerritories ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
