pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldDoNotOverdoCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Guideline 5: do not overdo it"@en, "Leitlinie 5: nicht übertreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Innerworld journeying has limits and dangers; when it becomes compulsive one should recall why one is doing it in the first place."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingHabitFormingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworld journeying is habit-forming"@en, "Innenweltreisen machen süchtig"@de ;
    skos:definition "The most obvious danger is habit: one may come to prefer the innerworld to surrounding life and lose balance and discrimination; being easy and solitary (book or tape) it can reinforce the cultural split between mind and body; it is a means, not an end."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworld journeying (pathworking)"@en, "Innenweltreise (Pfadarbeit)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enter a mythic mindscape through a guided imaginative journey, alone with a book or tape or in a group, following the six guidelines (consistency, sparse detail, challenge, map, moderation, record), with Centering before and after."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBPathworking (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node describes pathworking as a many-sensed story one steps into and identifies with; here innerworld journeying is entered under six guidelines with Centering before and after."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiEnhancedAwarenessInsightDeepMindAssociations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced awareness, insight and Deep Mind associations"@en, "Gesteigerte Bewusstheit, Einsicht und Assoziationen im Tiefen Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Innerworld travel is a tool, not a goal: it serves heightened awareness and insight and links chains of symbols and associations within the Deep Mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingYieldsAwarenessInsight a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworld journeying yields awareness and insight"@en, "Innenweltreisen bewirken Bewusstheit und Einsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Innerworld journeying is said to serve heightened awareness and insight and to link chains of symbols in the Deep Mind."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiEnhancedAwarenessInsightDeepMindAssociations ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
