pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldRecordEveryJourney a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Guideline 6: record every journey"@en, "Leitlinie 6: alle Reisen aufzeichnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Write down every journey, describing images, sights and encounters; this is stressed repeatedly as a discipline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGroundingProgressAssessmentThroughRecords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Grounding and progress assessment through records"@en, "Erdung und Fortschrittskontrolle durch Aufzeichnungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recording grounds experiences, gives a means to assess progress, embeds images in the mind and often recovers forgotten or unnoticed details."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondADiaryYieldsProgress (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node credits a record of practice with showing progress and keeping ideas for later; here the record of innerworld journeys is said to ground the experience, measure progress, fix the images and bring back forgotten details."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRecordKeepingYieldsGrounding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Record-keeping yields grounding"@en, "Aufzeichnen bewirkt Erdung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Writing down every journey is said to ground the experience and allow progress to be judged."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldRecordEveryJourney ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGroundingProgressAssessmentThroughRecords ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, Innerworld Explorations, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInsightNewCyclesChangeViaPathworking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insight and new cycles of change via pathworking"@en, "Einsicht und neue Wandlungszyklen durch Pfadarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pathworking lets one enter larger-than-life situations, take part in a mythic cycle and meet goddesses, spirits and beings, gaining new insights about self and world or starting fresh cycles of change and action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPathworkingYieldsListedCapacities a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Pathworking yields its listed capacities"@en, "Pfadarbeit bewirkt die genannten Fähigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pathworking is credited with insight, recovered oaths, sensory and animal exploration, death-rebirth, spirit relationships, intuition and discrimination."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBUsesPathworking (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node lists training, getting to know a belief system, identification and open spaces for scrying or enchantment; here the list is insight and new cycles of change, recovered oaths, sense and animal exploration, symbolic death and rebirth, spirit relations, intuition and discrimination."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInsightNewCyclesChangeViaPathworking, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRecoveringForgottenOathsConsciousDreamExploration, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExploringSensesAnimalShapesPathworking, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSymbolicDeathRebirth, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRelationshipsSpirits, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiIntuitionDiscriminationThroughPathworking, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSenseDiscrimination ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRecoveringForgottenOathsConsciousDreamExploration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recovering forgotten oaths and conscious dream exploration"@en, "Vergessene Gelübde wiederfinden und Träume bewusst erkunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through pathworkings one can consciously explore dream imagery, re-enter one's personal past and uncover oaths or promises to oneself that were forgotten or concealed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiExploringSensesAnimalShapesPathworking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Exploring senses and animal shapes in pathworking"@en, "Sinne und Tiergestalten in der Pfadarbeit erkunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "With music, incense or tastes one can see what images rise from the Deep Mind; one can take animal shapes, real or imaginary, discovering qualities beyond others' writings and correspondences."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSymbolicDeathRebirth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Symbolic death and rebirth"@en, "Symbolischer Tod und Wiedergeburt"@de ;
    skos:definition "In pathworking one can die periodically and be reborn, subtly altered by the experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRelationshipsSpirits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relationships with spirits"@en, "Beziehungen zu Geistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the innerworlds one can build relationships with all kinds of spirits, to be worked further into other magickal activity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiIntuitionDiscriminationThroughPathworking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intuition and discrimination through pathworking"@en, "Intuition und Unterscheidungsvermögen durch Pfadarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perhaps most importantly, pathworkings are said to help develop intuition and discernment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldBeingsMalignOrLyingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Innerworld beings may be malign or lie"@en, "Wesen der Innenwelt können bösartig sein oder lügen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not everything met in mindscapes is benevolent or truthful; our own capacity for self-deception and showing off appears there too; magickal systems tell of lying, distracting spirits and capricious ghosts; one needs a sense for the validity of an experience, and it helps to have someone to talk to."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCMisguides (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node warns of misleading spirits in the underworld of an initiatory crisis and counsels truthsense; here the warning concerns the mindscapes of pathworking, where one's own gift for self-deception reappears, and someone to talk to is advised."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiLyingSpiritsCapriciousGhostsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Lying spirits and capricious ghosts"@en, "Lügnerische Geister und launische Gespenster"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirits that deceive or distract careless travellers, and ghosts, said to be notoriously capricious, encountered in innerworlds."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBInhabitantsInnerworldsNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node names the spirits, demons and ancestors crowding the innerworlds; here only the lying spirits and capricious ghosts that mislead the unwary are named."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "spirits who lie", "ghosts" ;
    pm:nameRole "deceptive innerworld entities" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBeginningPathworkingsSelfKnowledge a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Beginning pathworkings from self-knowledge"@en, "Pfadarbeit beginnen mit Selbsterkenntnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Start with simple journeys built on images of what one knows about oneself: explore and map one's preferences, aversions, habits, fears, history and dreams and translate them into images as the basis for a journey."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMappingSelfBeforeChosenMindscapesPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Mapping the self before chosen mindscapes"@en, "Selbstkartierung vor gewählten Geisteslandschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "One needs readiness to explore and chart areas of the self; otherwise consciously chosen mindscapes may only further distort the gap between the self one would like to be and the self one actually is."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBeginningPathworkingsSelfKnowledge ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The mindscapes may merely deepen the distortion between the wished-for self-image and the actual self." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMindscapesDistortingSelfImageFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mindscapes distorting self-image"@en, "Geisteslandschaften verzerren das Selbstbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without self-mapping, pathworkings may further distort one's story of oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of pathworking begun without mapping the self, whose chosen mindscapes may only widen the gap between the wished-for and the actual self-image. No deadline; the rate word is may; the cause is put on the operator's skipped self-exploration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Exploring Our Mythic Worlds, How are Pathworkings Useful?, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .




#
# Axis Mundi
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAxisMundi a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Axis Mundi"@en, "Axis Mundi (Weltachse)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The central pivot of the shamanic cosmos, the point where all spheres meet, from which the shamanka begins every journey into any innerworld and performs magickal tasks; present in every shamanic and magickal system in guises such as the Warao sacred rattle, the Voudou crossroads, a ladder to the sky, world-tree, post, pillar or holy mountain."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAxisMundi (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node makes the axis less a place than a way of placing oneself, relaxed in the present; here it is the hub from which the shamanka starts every journey, shown through the Warao rattle, the Voudou crossroads and the world-tree, and only then an inner poise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCrossroadsSacredGodsNewYork a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Crossroads sacred to the Gods in New York"@en, "Kreuzungen in New York als den Göttern heilig"@de ;
    skos:definition "A contemporary Voudou practitioner is reported as describing every crossroads in New York City as sacred to the Gods; British folklore also gives crossroads magickal virtue."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine reports this from an unnamed contemporary practitioner of Voudou."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWorldTreeDerivatives a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "World-tree and its derivatives"@en, "Weltenbaum und seine Ableitungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world-tree image recurs worldwide; the author thinks the tree of knowledge in the Bible and the Qabalistic Otz Chaim likely derive from shamanic sources, and notes it in alchemy, Palaeolithic cave art and tantrik iconography."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBTreeLifeShamanicWorldTree (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node holds that the Tree of Life of the Qabalah likely grew from a shamanic world-tree; here the Biblical tree of knowledge is added and the image is traced in alchemy, Palaeolithic cave painting and tantrik iconography."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShamanismRootMagick a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanism as the root of magick"@en, "Schamanismus als Wurzel der Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanism is said to be the root of magick and of art, dance, theatre and philosophy; every magickal system has shamanic elements."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAxisMundiInnerPoise a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Axis Mundi as inner poise"@en, "Axis Mundi als innere Ausgewogenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the practitioner the Axis Mundi is also an inner state, the pivot of inner life: a matter of poise, equilibrium and inner balance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShamanicWorkTaxingCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic work is taxing"@en, "Schamanische Arbeit ist anstrengend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanic work can be very demanding mentally and physically, with periodic psychic crises and descents into the underworld."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalancePoise ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInitiatoryCrisesNotSacredMadness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiatory crises, not sacred madness"@en, "Initiatorische Krisen statt heiligen Wahnsinns"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine rejects the popular view of the shaman as an outsider set apart by a madness held sacred, finding little evidence for it: psychic crises, vocational illness and descents through creative derangement are needed passages, high points of initiation, through which the shamanka gains her poise."@en ;
    skos:note "Only Hine's side is read; the view he rejects is called a popular misconception and has no named holder."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInitiatoryTrialsBeforePoiseJourneyPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiatory trials before poise to journey"@en, "Initiatorische Prüfungen vor der Fähigkeit zu reisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is through crises and initiatory ordeals that the shamanka gains the balance needed to journey between worlds and work with spirits."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as the way poise arises, not as an instruction; no consequence of its absence is given."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInitiatoryCrisesNotSacredMadness ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalancePoise ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalancePoise a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner balance and poise"@en, "Inneres Gleichgewicht und Ausgewogenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Poise and balance needed to travel between worlds and deal with spirits; said to be developed through initiatory trials and through Centering exercises."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBBeingCentredPoised (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is the relaxed readiness of being centred; here poise is what lets the shamanka travel between worlds and deal with spirits, won through initiatory trials as well as through Centering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiEliadeCuredSickMan a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eliade on the cured sick man"@en, "Eliade über den geheilten Kranken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoted: initiatory maladies accompany the medicine-man's vocation because, like the sick man, he is projected onto a plane revealing solitude, danger and hostility; but the shaman is chiefly an ill person who healed himself."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine quotes Eliade's classic work on shamanism at length; the node holds his quotation, and Eliade is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSloppyShamanismFoolishCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sloppy shamanism is foolish"@en, "Schlampiger Schamanismus ist töricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is a misconception that shamanic techniques spare one rigorous practice like yoga or visualising; a haphazard approach because shamanic magick seems spontaneous is called foolishness; sloppy shamans would not survive in the wild world."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalancePoise ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalanceRequiredBeShamanPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner balance required to be a shaman"@en, "Inneres Gleichgewicht als Voraussetzung des Schamanentums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Legends across shamanic cultures stress that not just anyone is a shaman: it requires inner balance, whether climbing a knife ladder or crossing an abyss on a single hair."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent step stands for the shamanic journey between the worlds as this volume teaches it; no consequence beyond the legendary ordeals is given."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalancePoise ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringAliasBanishing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering, alias banishing"@en, "Zentrierung, auch Bannung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Work that develops balance is called Centering; in post-Golden Dawn Western magick it is called banishing, the best known being the lesser banishing ritual of the pentagram, which the author does not describe; its principles matter: a banishing opens and closes every working."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBanishingOpensClosesEachWorkingPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Banishing opens and closes each working"@en, "Bannung zu Beginn und Ende jeder Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Western ritual magick places a banishing at the start and close of each working, whether full ritual, innerworld journey or meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBBanishing (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 practice says a banishing is done before and after working; here this is given as the rule of Western ritual magick for every kind of working, from full ritual to meditation."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringExerciseGeneralForm ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringExerciseGeneralForm a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering exercise (general form)"@en, "Zentrierungsübung (allgemeine Form)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most Centering exercises share three elements done in order: (1) mark out the area as sacred space; (2) symbolically order the zones, gates or directions of one's magickal universe, whose centre becomes the Axis Mundi; (3) identify with a chosen inspiring source, merging macrocosm and microcosm. Symbols are one's own choice but must be meaningful and consistent with the system one works in. Done before the main activity, repeated afterwards as Grounding; may also be practised on its own."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice opens with attention to one's bodily presence; here the first element is marking out a sacred space, and the symbols must fit the system in use."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringThreePartsSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Three parts of Centering"@en, "Drei Teile der Zentrierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The source orders Centering as three stages: casting the circle, ordering the magickal universe, identification with the source."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBCentering (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice lists three elements whose first is attention to bodily presence; here the three stages are casting the circle, ordering the magickal universe and identification with the source."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCastingCircle ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiOrderingMagickalUniverse ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiIdentificationPrimalSource ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine gives the shared elements of Centering in a fixed order: the space is first marked as sacred, then its zones or directions are ordered so that its centre becomes the Axis Mundi, and only from that centre does one identify with the chosen source; each stage takes its sense from standing on the one before." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCastingCircle a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Casting the Circle"@en, "Den Kreis ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Define the working space as sacred: e.g. decorate the circle by quarter (Sheila Broun's method): incense or feathers with blue for air in the east, candles and red objects for fire in the south, shells and water for the west, stones and crystals in the north; or sweep it out, set up staves carved with totem-animal heads, mark the boundary with ash, chalk, flour or cord, or lay down patterned cloth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSheilaBrounsAccountHerCircleReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Sheila Broun's account of her circle"@en, "Sheila Brouns Bericht über ihren Kreis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author presents a quoted passage in Sheila Broun's own words describing how she creates and decorates her circles."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Phil Hine" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Sheila Broun" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Quoted by Hine as Broun's own account of how she casts and decorates her circles, under the first part of Centering." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiOrderingMagickalUniverse a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ordering the magickal universe"@en, "Das magische Universum ordnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mark out the universe's basic elements in the space, from the four cardinal directions to complex arrays of gates and tunnels; in the usual Western form the magician takes the central position and focuses on each direction as physical direction, inner quality and spiritual force, e.g. calling the four winds, four archangels, Hindu elemental stewards or Wiccan watchtowers; some systems use eight directions; place elemental Power Objects at the matching points."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAccessingAnyPartUniverseAxisMundi a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accessing any part of the universe from the Axis Mundi"@en, "Von der Weltachse aus jeden Teil des Universums erreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the sacred space mirrors the wider universe, moving to its centre, in effect the Axis Mundi, is said to let one reach or affect any region of the cosmos."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFourArchangelsFourWindsElementalStewardsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Four archangels, four winds, elemental stewards, watchtowers"@en, "Vier Erzengel, vier Winde, Elementarverwalter, Wachtürme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beings called upon at the four quarters in centering in different systems: the four winds (Greek), four great archangels (Qabalah), elemental stewards (Hindu), four watchtowers (Wicca)."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "four winds", "four archangels", "elemental stewards", "watchtowers" ;
    pm:nameRole "guardians/forces of the four directions" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWatchtowersDeesEnochianMagick a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Watchtowers from Dee's Enochian magick"@en, "Wachtürme aus Dees henochischer Magie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The four watchtowers of Wicca are said to originate in the Enochian magick of the Elizabethan magus Dr John Dee."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiIdentificationPrimalSource a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Identification with the primal source"@en, "Identifikation mit der Urquelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adopt the attitude of union with whatever image one holds of the primal source of energy: Tao, Void, the Great Spirit, or a deity of either sex."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPrimalSourceImagesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Primal source images"@en, "Bilder der Urquelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Images of primal source energy with which one identifies in the third part of Centering: Tao, Void, the Great Spirit, or a deity of either sex."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the Great Spirit", "Goddess", "God", "Tao", "Void" ;
    pm:nameRole "primal source energy" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiIncongruentCenteringSymbolsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Incongruent centering symbols"@en, "Unstimmige Zentrierungssymbole"@de ;
    skos:definition "Symbols must fit the system in use: a Qabalistic centering in Celtic shamanic work would be incongruous; they should be powerful for the practitioner since the Deep Mind is stirred by centering."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringExerciseGeneralForm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringAssociationChainIntoDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering as an association chain into the Deep Mind"@en, "Zentrierung als Assoziationskette in den Tiefen Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calling a spirit in a quarter links a chain: physical qualities of the element, its psychological qualities, its spiritual energies, associated myths; this binds social, mythic and personal experience, reaches archetypal experience in the Deep Mind and releases energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBalancingAspectsSelfIntoDynamicWhole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Balancing aspects of self into a dynamic whole"@en, "Die Aspekte des Selbst zu einem dynamischen Ganzen ausbalancieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each part of Centering is said to balance the self's different aspects into a more dynamic whole, growing more effective with each repetition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringYieldsBalance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Centering yields balance"@en, "Zentrierung bewirkt Gleichgewicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each part of Centering is said to bring the aspects of the self into balance as a livelier whole and to build poise."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCenteringYieldsPoiseYield (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node credits Centering with relaxation and readiness for action; here it balances the parts of the self into a dynamic whole and builds the poise to journey."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringExerciseGeneralForm ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBalancingAspectsSelfIntoDynamicWhole, pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerBalancePoise ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCenteringBecomesIncreasinglyEffectiveSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Centering becomes increasingly effective"@en, "Zentrierung wird zunehmend wirksamer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each repetition is said to make it more effective."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of Centering, which grows more effective with each performance. No measure of effectiveness is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUsingPowerSpotAxisMundi a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using a Power Spot as Axis Mundi"@en, "Einen Kraftort als Weltachse nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one has a power spot, use it as one's Axis Mundi, allowing a much simpler centering exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiComplexSimplerCenteringConfidence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "From complex to simpler centering with confidence"@en, "Mit wachsendem Vertrauen von komplexer zu einfacher Zentrierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author began with complex rituals like the Lesser Pentagram rite and moved to simpler exercises as his confidence grew; complexity is a matter of taste and confidence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGroundingAfterWorkEssentialPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Grounding after work is essential"@en, "Erdung nach der Arbeit ist unerlässlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeating Centering after the main work is called essential; otherwise a vision from the work may erupt unbidden during everyday activities."@en ;
    skos:note "Read as: the safe close of a scrying session or journey presupposes grounding; in time the grounding comes after the work."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCentredAndReturning (Oven-Ready Chaos, text of 1992): the 1992 node says the repeated centering readies a return to consensus reality; here grounding is called essential and the consequence of skipping it, visions breaking into daily life, is given with a friend's case."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGrounding ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicCondBScrying, pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiInnerworldJourneyingPathworking ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Sudden visions from the work may intrude into everyday life, as in the driving anecdote." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUnwantedIntrusionTranceMaterialCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unwanted intrusion of trance material"@en, "Unerwünschtes Eindringen von Trancematerial"@de ;
    skos:definition "Just as everyday thoughts distract trancework, visions from magickal work erupting in daily life are undesirable unless intended."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGrounding ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 35; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiGrounding a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Grounding"@en, "Erdung"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the main activity repeat the Centering exercise to bring oneself back to earth, restoring equilibrium so poise and balance are kept."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcCentredAndReturning (Oven-Ready Chaos, text of 1992): the 1992 node says the repeated centering readies a return to consensus reality; here the repetition is named Grounding and said to restore equilibrium so that poise is kept."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 35; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUngroundedScryerFloodedImagesWhileDrivingFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ungrounded scryer flooded with images while driving"@en, "Ungeerdete Seherin beim Autofahren von Bildern überflutet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A clairvoyant friend who neglected grounding after scrying was flooded with hypnagogic-like images on glancing in her rear-view mirror while driving next morning; she kept control and stopped, but in heavy traffic it could have ended badly."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of a working left ungrounded; a clairvoyant friend who skipped grounding after scrying was flooded with images at the wheel the next morning. The delay is stated (the next morning); no rate; the cause is put on the operator's neglect. Hine reports it from the friend, and the outcome was a near miss."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 35; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMagickStirsDeepMindPeriodsImbalance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick stirs the Deep Mind; periods of imbalance"@en, "Magie rührt den Tiefen Geist auf; Phasen des Ungleichgewichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "All magickal work rouses the Deep Mind and brings aspects of psyche forward; periods of imbalance are inevitable for growth and should be recognised and opened to, while distinguishing between drowning in them and knowing they are a passage to come through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 35; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDoNotDrownImbalanceCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not drown in imbalance"@en, "Nicht im Ungleichgewicht ertrinken"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is a difference between being totally overwhelmed by a period of imbalance and knowing it as a necessary time to pass through and come out of."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMagickStirsDeepMindPeriodsImbalance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Axis Mundi, Centering, p. 35; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .




#
# Power Objects
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPowerObjects a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power Objects"@en, "Kraftgegenstände"@de ;
    skos:definition "Physical aids to the practitioner, called Magickal Weapons or Tools in Western magick and Power Objects in modern shamanism: crystals, drums, bullroarers, rattles and anything used as an aid; some traditional, some found objects."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiEthicallyHarmfulTradeShamanicArtefactsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ethically harmful trade in shamanic artefacts"@en, "Ethisch schädlicher Handel mit schamanischen Artefakten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The market for authentic-looking artefacts can go to extremes: rare American birds are said to be hunted for New Age objects, and crystals are dug by underpaid, poorly protected workers in poor countries."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPowerObjects ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMakePowerObjectsYourself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Make power objects yourself; looks do not matter"@en, "Kraftgegenstände selbst machen; das Aussehen zählt nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against the assumption that shamanic objects must look ethnic, much favours making them from what is to hand (a Venezuelan shaman's altar held a bayonet, a cutlass and a tin-can rattle); fixed ideas of what a tool should look like obstruct; it matters only that they work for you."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiMakingImprovisedMusicalInstrument a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making an improvised musical instrument"@en, "Ein improvisiertes Musikinstrument bauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanic Development Course project: each participant makes one or more musical instruments before the following weekly session; one participant first declared it impossible owing to fixed ideas of what an instrument is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRattle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Rattle"@en, "Die Rassel"@de ;
    skos:definition "In some cultures the rattle is the central axis, used to summon spirits and Gods; its handle is the world-tree climbed in trance, its head the sky domain of ancestors and spirits; it may symbolise purifying fire, used in healing to counter fever heat; the Warao community rattle of sacred wood and mythic gourd emits sparks when whirled, as crystals inside ignite wood particles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Rattle, p. 37; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSummoningSpiritsGodsRattle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Summoning spirits and Gods with the rattle"@en, "Geister und Götter mit der Rassel herbeirufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamans use the rattle to call spirits and deities, and in some cultures in healing rites against fever."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Rattle, p. 37; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFlute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Flute"@en, "Die Flöte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Found in nearly all shamanic cultures, made of bone, bamboo, reed or sacred wood; seen as channels for spirit voices, often linked to bird-spirits; sometimes phallic, used in male initiations (taboo for New Guinea women and children to see), while the Thompson River whistle was a women's sacred instrument; sometimes paired male/female; Greeks saw it as healing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Flute, p. 37; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiHealingFluteDemocritus a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing with the flute (Democritus)"@en, "Heilen mit der Flöte (Demokrit)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Democritus is reported to have recommended the flute to cure many ailments including snakebite."@en ;
    skos:note "Hine reports Democritus' advice; it is not read through him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Flute, p. 38; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDrumRhythm a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Drum and rhythm"@en, "Die Trommel und der Rhythmus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drumming is a leading route to ecstatic states; rhythms propel listeners and drummers into trance and changes of beat shift trance awareness through the ritual; cultures keep specific ceremonial rhythms (Voudou drumming schools); rhythm structures time-sense, cues movement with less effort (marching band study), becomes a motor attitude freeing attention, and is mirrored by brain activity and heart rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCRhythmAndDelivery (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node treats rhythm for invocatory delivery and verse; here rhythm is treated through the shamanic drum, with ceremonial rhythm batteries, the marching-band finding and the mirroring of rhythm by brain and heart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Drum, p. 38; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTranceThroughDrumming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trance through drumming"@en, "Trance durch Trommeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drum rhythms are said to carry both listeners and drummers into trance and to shift trance awareness to different phases of a ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Drum, p. 38; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiDrummingYieldsTrance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Drumming yields trance"@en, "Trommeln bewirkt Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drum rhythms are said to carry listeners and drummers into trance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShamanicDrummingTrance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTranceThroughDrumming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
