pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiShamanicDrummingTrance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic drumming for trance"@en, "Schamanisches Trommeln zur Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drum (or listen to drumming) with specific rhythms to enter trance, changing beats to move trance awareness between parts of a ritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, The Drum, p. 38; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSaltCleansing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Salt in cleansing"@en, "Salz bei Reinigungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salt readily picks up psychic energy and, dissolved in water, lets the water be more readily charged; hence its use in cleansing rituals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Crystals, p. 39; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiHuicholCrystalAncestralShamanNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Huichol crystal as ancestral shaman"@en, "Huichol-Kristall als Ahnenschamane"@de ;
    skos:definition "Among the Huichol the crystal is held to be an ancestral shaman who came back from the sky world as light made solid, to live among his kin as guardian and guiding spirit; the notion of crystals as condensed spirit is widespread from America to Australia."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "crystal (Huichol)" ;
    pm:nameRole "ancestral shaman, guardian and guiding spirit" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Crystals, p. 39; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiWaraoFamilyFamiliarsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Warao family of familiars"@en, "Warao-Familie der Vertrauten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The crystals in the Warao sacred rattle are called the familiars that form the shaman's family."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "family of familiars" ;
    pm:nameRole "familiar spirits housed in rattle crystals" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Crystals, p. 39; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSoulBones a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Soul in the bones"@en, "Die Seele in den Knochen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A widespread shamanic belief places the vital force or soul in the bones rather than the flesh, which makes bone a sacred material for power objects; bone hunting rituals, skeletal underworld figures and Tantric bone headdresses, bowls and thigh-bone trumpets are cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Bone, p. 39; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFoundObjectsShamansEqualFootingEnvironment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Found objects and the shaman's equal footing with environment"@en, "Fundstücke und die Gleichrangigkeit des Schamanen mit der Umwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The shaman uses any part of the environment, giving it sacred purpose, from the premise that she stands equal with animals, plants and spirits as a participant in the world; adopting a shamanic outlook means seeking the sacred everywhere, including machines and cities."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBGivens (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node concerns givens and found objects kept until a use appears; here found objects show the shaman's premise of equal footing with all of the environment and the call to seek the sacred everywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 39; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPlacingSpiritInPowerObject a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making or finding a Power Object and placing a spirit in it"@en, "Einen Kraftgegenstand machen oder finden und einen Geist hineinsetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make or find an object and place a spirit in it, ceremonially or informally, as a start to seeing the sacred everywhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTalismanicLuckObject a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Talismanic luck object"@en, "Talismanischer Glücksgegenstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "The simplest power object, of the kind of a lucky rabbit's foot, builds a talismanic association and may be said to hold a spirit increasing one's personal power or luck."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFindingLostThings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding lost things"@en, "Verlorenes wiederfinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "A figure treated as a spirit-person is credited with finding lost items."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBFindingLostObjects (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node finds lost things by divination; here they are found by a spirit housed in a figure treated as a person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUnthankedGnomeTurnsMischievousFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unthanked Gnome turns mischievous"@en, "Unbedankter Gnom wird schelmisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "If people did not thank him, the Gnome reportedly grew mischievous, hiding things that later surfaced in odd places."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of the finding spirit, which grew mischievous and hid things when people did not thank it. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the user's neglected courtesy, not on the spirit's power."@en, "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBFindingPixie (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 practice reports only the asking and thanking; here neglecting the thanks is said to turn the spirit mischievous."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTreatingToolsSpiritInhabited a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Treating tools as spirit-inhabited"@en, "Werkzeuge als von Geistern bewohnt behandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treat inanimate objects, especially personalised tools such as cars, as independent entities or homes for spirits, with due respect and reverence; sing to and offer gifts to power objects as shamans do; avoid dogmatism (e.g. incense by a computer)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRespectSpiritsPlacedObjectsAvoidDogmatismCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Respect spirits placed in objects; avoid dogmatism"@en, "Geister in Gegenständen respektieren; Dogmatismus vermeiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "If placing spirits into objects, treating them with respect and reverence is held wise; but one should not be dogmatic, as incense near a computer will not please."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiPlacingSpiritInPowerObject ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiChangedRelationshipObjectsBenefitLivingTools a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Changed relationship with objects; benefit from living tools"@en, "Veränderte Beziehung zu Gegenständen; Nutzen lebendiger Werkzeuge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating objects as spirit-homes is said to change one's relationship to them surprisingly; treating power objects as living entities with some volition is said to benefit one greatly and the gift-giving habit pays off."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTreatingToolsAliveYieldsBenefit a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Treating tools as alive yields benefit"@en, "Werkzeuge als lebendig behandeln bringt Nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating one's tools as living, spirit-inhabited things is said to change one's relation to them and to repay one well."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiTreatingToolsSpiritInhabited ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiChangedRelationshipObjectsBenefitLivingTools ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAncientPowerObjectsFamiliars a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ancient power objects with familiars"@en, "Alte Kraftgegenstände mit eigenen Vertrauten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Very old power objects are said sometimes to possess familiars of their own, having gained mythic significance from owners and years of use; power objects are extensions of oneself and one's cosmology."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Power Objects, Found Objects, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .




#
# Drawing Threads Together
#
pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiCombiningWorldsIntoProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Combining the worlds into one process"@en, "Die Welten zu einem Prozess verbinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "All techniques can be used separately, but the closing example shows how ways of exploring each world combine and interweave into a whole process; it is developed from unpublished work of Neil McLachlan."@en ;
    skos:note "The closing example is said to be developed from unpublished work of Neil McLachlan."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFiveElementsCircle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five elements on the circle"@en, "Fünf Elemente im Kreis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fire, Air, Water and Earth relate to the cardinal directions (South, East, West, North) on the circle, a symbol of totality, with the fifth element, spirit, tao or void, at the centre."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalExplorationSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental exploration through the three worlds"@en, "Elementerkundung durch die drei Welten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The source orders a series of steps working through Personal, Mythic and Social worlds: correspondences and meditation, shield, becoming the element at power spots, seeking tokens, fusing tokens, using tokens."@en ;
    skos:note "The closing example is said to be developed from unpublished work of Neil McLachlan; the six steps are taken in order through the Personal, Mythic and Social worlds."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalCorrespondencesMeditation ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalShield ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBecomingElementAtItsPlace ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSeekingElementalTokens ;
    rdf:_5 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFusingPlaceAndToken ;
    rdf:_6 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiUsingElementalTokens ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The elemental exploration runs from reading and meditating on correspondences, through a shield of the insights, becoming each element at its place, asking each place for a token and fusing token and place, to using the tokens; each step builds on what the one before has made, so the tokens are gates only after the places have been known and fused into them." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalCorrespondencesMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental exploration 1: correspondences and meditation"@en, "Elementerkundung 1: Entsprechungen und Meditation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gather the book correspondences of each element, then meditate on each, recognising by which qualities it contributes to oneself (relating the elements to one's Personal world); scrying may help the meditation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiElementalShield a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental exploration 2: elemental shield"@en, "Elementerkundung 2: Elementeschild"@de ;
    skos:definition "From these insights make one or several shields depicting how the elements interrelate inside oneself, e.g. a circle in four elemental parts with spirit in the middle and also outside the rim; develop it further over time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBecomingElementAtItsPlace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental exploration 3: becoming the element at its power spot"@en, "Elementerkundung 3: an seinem Kraftort zum Element werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Find places where each element predominates (an exposed windy place for air, a beach or spit for water, a spot to build an undisturbed fire, a mountain, hill slope or fertile vale for earth, a quiet indoor place or a starry night outdoors for void); there drop preconceptions, let the element's feeling flood through, try to become it, let the mind roam over all its appearances and earliest memories of it (e.g. candle flames to reactor fire), notice how it appears in one's life; for void, contemplate its expressions in religions and feel it as the deep centre of self and all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiAwarenessPowerSpotsElementalExplorationPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of Power Spots for elemental exploration"@en, "Kenntnis der Kraftorte für die Elementerkundung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coming to know the elements one after another requires being aware of Power Spots."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFindingPowerSpotsIncongruitiesTerrain ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiBecomingElementAtItsPlace ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiSeekingElementalTokens a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental exploration 4: seeking elemental tokens"@en, "Elementerkundung 4: Elementtoken suchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Return to each place of meditation and ask the element for a token or gift, open to omens; it may be found, given, or catch one's eye in a shop (pebble or crystal for earth, feathers for air, charred wood for fire, shell or driftwood for water; for void a unique or black object, or a recognisable meditative calm)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTwiRecognisingTokenSpecialSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising the token as special"@en, "Den Token als besonders erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "How the token arrives does not matter; the sign is one's awareness that the thing is special."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of seeking an elemental token, the seeker's awareness that the object is special however it arrived. Only the seeker's own recognition checks it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TwoWorldsAndInbetween ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Two Worlds and Inbetween: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume II (Pagan News Publications, chapbook, 1989; on-line version of June 1999), Drawing Threads Together, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 2_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTwiFusingPlaceAndToken a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Elemental exploration 5: fusing place and token"@en, "Elementerkundung 5: Ort und Token verschmelzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With all five objects, return to the elemental places, let each element's experience flood through again while holding the token so the energies pass through oneself into it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
