#
# Volume 3: Touched by Fire
#

#
# prima-materia — chaos magic: Hine, Touched by Fire (Techniques of Modern Shamanism, vol. 3)
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:ChaosMagic (pmw:TouchedByFire).
# Edition: Phil Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Vol. 3,
# copyright line "Phil Hine 1989, Pagan News Publication", in the Acrobat
# conversion of March 1998. Read complete in the full-text layer of the
# archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-
# collection, file "Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt",
# 73759 characters. Pages 10-44 stand as bare number lines at the foot of each
# page; pp. 5-9 carry none and are cited from the page breaks of the layout and
# the contents page, marked as inferred. The text refers to the summer of 1989
# as last year and to 9 April 1990, so the 1989 of the copyright line is cited
# as printed and not corrected.
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#893 with two independent extraction passes,
# reconciled by offset and word overlap, then integrated by a third reader of
# the whole text, who added the nodes whose note says so. Every record was
# compared with the Hine nodes of Condensed Chaos, Oven-Ready Chaos, Prime
# Chaos, The Pseudonomicon and Aspects of Evocation; a node on the same topic
# in another form carries a note beginning "Differs from". Where Hine reports
# another author (Mace, Campbell, Keel, Reich, Starhawk), the node holds his
# ascription and the named work is not read through him. Signs of success,
# outcome reports and conditions of failure carry a note beginning "Counted
# as a sign of success:", "Counted as an outcome report:" or "Counted as a
# condition of failure:".
#
#
# Introduction
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfShamanismAsCommunityFunction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic work as a community function"@en, "Schamanische Arbeit als Gemeinschaftsfunktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanic work is framed less as a personal journey and more as recovering a functional role a person can come to play within their community."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Introduction, p. 5 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNonPrescriptiveApproach a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-prescriptive approach of the book"@en, "Nicht-präskriptiver Ansatz des Buches"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author states the book is not a training manual and offers no set solutions, only approaches to situations, which he holds to be more flexible; some passages are meant as atmospheric text that approaches its point obliquely, and many techniques are named but not described, leaving follow-up to the reader."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the methods are; author adds he still feels a novice after 14 years of training."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Introduction, p. 5 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfMagickAsSurvival a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magick as a survival technology"@en, "Magie als Überlebenstechnik"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author treats magick as a means of improving survival in one's surroundings, rural or inner-city; shamanism is said to have arisen from early human strategies for survival and evolution, and a shamanic outlook is offered as help for a needed evolutionary leap."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Introduction, p. 5 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAgainstWorkshopShamanism a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Satire of the weekend-workshop shamanism scene"@en, "Satire auf die Wochenend-Workshop-Schamanismusszene"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author mocks the route of training under a famous name, collecting titles, adding the word shamanic to an alternative therapy and adopting a New Age name, as a way of becoming an urban shaman."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed party: the commercial neo-shamanic workshop scene (tradition, not a named author)."@en, "Entered as a concept: only Hine's side is read; the workshop scene he mocks is not cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 7 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBecomingUsefulPerson a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a useful person in a community"@en, "Zu einer nützlichen Person in der Gemeinschaft werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Embed yourself in a community until people send others to you with problems; when someone confides an uncanny experience, reassure them that such things are common and not a sign of madness, perhaps telling of a similar case you know of; be available to look at disturbances in homes, give tarot readings and talk about intrusions of the uncanny."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 7 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfUsefulPersonStanding a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognised standing as the community's useful person"@en, "Anerkannte Stellung als nützliche Person der Gemeinschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "A role in which members of one's community seek one out for help with uncanny or practical troubles; presented as one way of developing a shamanic stance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 8 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfUsefulPersonYieldsStanding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Embedding in community yields useful-person standing"@en, "Einbettung in die Gemeinschaft ergibt die Stellung als nützliche Person"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living in a community as someone others are sent to, and reassuring those who confide uncanny experiences, is said to bring standing as the community's useful person."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBecomingUsefulPerson ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfUsefulPersonStanding ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
