pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHauntedHouseVigilOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Haunted-house vigil followed by people seeking the author out"@en, "Nachtwache im Spukhaus, danach suchten Leute den Autor auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the author stayed overnight in a well-known haunted house with its last remaining resident, word spread and people began to ask him to look at things in their homes and read tarot for them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, not as a sign announced in advance: after Hine stayed a night in a well-known haunted house with its last resident, people began to seek him out to look at things in their homes and to read the Tarot for them; he puts it down to word on the grapevine, and nothing separates the vigil from other reasons people might have come."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 8 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHandlingPostedCurse a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Handling a curse sent through the post"@en, "Umgang mit einem per Post geschickten Fluch"@de ;
    skos:definition "For someone threatened by phone and sent a curse object: first set up protection for everyone involved; support it with magickal counselling covering how they can protect themselves, how the curse works and which signs to watch for; lastly tackle the curse directly and, where traceable, those who sent it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 8 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCurseHandlingYieldsProtection a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Curse-handling procedure yields curse protection"@en, "Fluchbehandlung ergibt Fluchschutz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Protecting those involved, counselling them and then dealing with the curse itself is offered as the way to shield people from a curse and neutralise it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHandlingPostedCurse ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCurseProtection ;
