pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCurseProtection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Protection against and neutralising of curses"@en, "Schutz vor Flüchen und deren Unschädlichmachung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to protect cursed persons and to deal with a curse and its senders."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 8 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAmateurCursesWorkCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Amateur curses can still work"@en, "Auch Fluchen von Amateuren kann wirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns that curse work is more widespread than expected and that being done mostly by amateurs does not make it ineffective."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHandlingPostedCurse ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 8 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychicAttackSelfInduced a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Most psychic attack is self-induced and comes from intimates"@en, "Die meisten psychischen Angriffe sind selbst herbeigeführt und gehen von Nahestehenden aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that most psychic attack is self-generated: belief that a hostile lodge is sending harm becomes self-fulfilling even if the lodge does not exist; in his experience most real attacks come from people the victim knows, such as former or current lovers."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondAKarmaTidesExcusesFailure (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node treats psychic attack as an excuse invoked when magic goes wrong; here most psychic attack is self-induced through belief in a hostile lodge, and the real cases mostly come from people the victim knows."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 8 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychicAttackLifeThreateningCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Psychic attack can endanger life"@en, "Psychischer Angriff kann lebensgefährlich sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Psychic attack may threaten life when the victim turns suicidal or grows confused enough to walk in front of traffic; one must know how to deal with it, not merely recognise its signs."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychicAttackSelfInduced ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfConversionPrayerAttackCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forced conversion prayer as psychic attack"@en, "Erzwungenes Bekehrungsgebet als psychischer Angriff"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pagans prayed over in relays by born-again groups, or exorcised and called possessed or mad by family or friends, are said by the author to suffer psychic attack equal to a pin-stuck poppet; having a new belief system battered by someone certain of being right can cause severe trauma."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychicAttackSelfInduced ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEclecticAdaptablePractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eclectic, adaptable practice"@en, "Eklektische, anpassungsfähige Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because approaches to magick are endlessly plural, the author does not keep to one system; being eclectic and adaptable to new situations is said to be more useful to him."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondADiverseApproaches (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node says chaos magicians may draw on any system and so agree little among themselves; here eclecticism is Hine's own working choice, grounded in the plurality of magic met in suburbs and estates and the need to adapt to new situations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingClients a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing of clients"@en, "Heilung von Klienten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to help clients with health and personal problems by shamanic means; the author calls it the hardest part of his work."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBMagicalHealing (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node names magical healing of clients as needing further investigation; here healing is the hardest part of Hine's community work, done with counselling, trance, body energies and spirits, and bounded by referral."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAdmitLimitsReferOnCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Admit limits and refer on"@en, "Grenzen eingestehen und weiterverweisen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In healing it is wise to tell a person you do not know a field in detail and to recommend someone who does; training in conventional medicine is useful when people ask about their drugs."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingRepertoire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingRepertoire a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic healing repertoire"@en, "Repertoire schamanischen Heilens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Healing work combines counselling, inducing trance, body-energy work, instruction in relaxation and centering, getting spirits to look after particular problems and sometimes ritual; match the approach to the client, since some prefer full ritual and others light trance with few trappings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingRepertoireYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Healing repertoire yields healing"@en, "Heilrepertoire ergibt Heilung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine's mixed repertoire of counselling, trance, body-energy work, relaxation teaching and spirits is the means by which he helps clients with health problems."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingRepertoire ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingClients ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 9 (unmarked in the text layer; inferred from the page sequence); read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTurningCursesBack a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning curses back on their senders"@en, "Flüche auf ihre Absender zurückwenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Retributive work in which a curse is returned to those who sent it; given as the prime example of the shaman stepping into murky situations."@en ;
    skos:note "Procedure not detailed in this volume."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCarThievesDreamOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Car thieves frightened through their dreams"@en, "Autodiebe in ihren Träumen erschreckt"@de ;
    skos:definition "For a friend whose stolen car came back without sentimental items, the author arranged things so that the friend himself frightened the thieves by appearing in their dreams."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, not as a sign announced in advance: Hine says he arranged things so that the friend himself frightened the car thieves by appearing in their dreams; the method is not given, and no report from the thieves is mentioned."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfRetributionNotLightlyCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Retribution never to be done lightly"@en, "Vergeltung nie leichtfertig betreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says such cases are rare and that these activities should never be undertaken casually."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTurningCursesBack ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFindingPointOfPower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding one's point of power in a situation"@en, "Den eigenen Kraftpunkt in einer Situation finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "On entering a new situation, determine the role you will play in how events unfold, whether open support or quiet prompting behind the scenes; once found, keep to that point, since it is the best place from which to influence matters; first search for loopholes where a situation looks hopeless; extreme cases demand extreme tactics."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPointOfPowerYieldsInfluence a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Point of power yields influence"@en, "Kraftpunkt ergibt Einfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping to the role found on entering a situation is said to be the best way for Hine to influence how it unfolds."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFindingPointOfPower ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInfluenceOverSituation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInfluenceOverSituation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Effective influence over a situation"@en, "Wirksamer Einfluss auf eine Situation"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to influence an unfolding situation from a chosen position."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 10; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSituationsOutstripPrescriptions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Situations outstrip prescriptions"@en, "Situationen übersteigen Rezepte"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that real situations always exceed existing recipes, and that the complexity of city work outstrips current magical realities, which may connect one to tradition or archetypes but do not help with urban wild cards such as a young addict needing to detox."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed methods can be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPerspectiveOnOwnConflicts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Perspective on one's own conflicts"@en, "Abstand zu den eigenen Konflikten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Encountering other people's real horrors is said to be instructive, keeping one from inflating personal inner conflicts into cosmic disasters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInterventionAddictionCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Intervention as addiction"@en, "Eingreifen als Sucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intervening can itself become addictive; once you persuade yourself you are a shaman or healer and nurse that thought, you may rush in and make things worse, as with an acquaintance who hugged everyone regardless of body language; examine the circumstances, those involved and your own state before acting."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-directed warning against the practitioner role itself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFindingPointOfPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHelpMakesWorseFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Situations where any help makes things worse"@en, "Situationen, in denen jede Hilfe schadet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sooner or later a situation arises in which nothing you do helps and trying only worsens it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of intervention, in the situation where whatever one does cannot help and trying only makes it worse; Hine says one will meet such a case sooner or later. No deadline and no rate beyond that certainty; the cause is put on the situation, the harm on a helper who will not stop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInformationGathering a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Information-gathering"@en, "Informationssammlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Collect as much information as possible from any source at all, spirits as well as social services staff, treating every datum as potentially useful even when it seems unrelated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCitiesAsMyths a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cities as myths spawning demons and elementals"@en, "Städte als Mythen, die Dämonen und Elementare hervorbringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cities are described as self-rewriting myths that breed demons such as incest, rape, abuse, drugs and poverty, beside which any spirit lured into a triangle is trivial; urban life is said to generate odd elementals and partly sentient energy nexuses that magic has barely begun to address."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 11; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfShamanicVocation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shaman's work as vocation repaid in love and trust"@en, "Schamanische Arbeit als Berufung, vergolten durch Liebe und Vertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamans are said to help their community survive and develop, which also aids their own progress; the author suspects it is a vocation whose reward is love, support and mutual trust."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Personal Reflections on Urban Shamanism, p. 12; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Staking out the Territory: roles; Sorcerer
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfShamanicRoles a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic roles"@en, "Schamanische Rollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine lists roles a shamanic practitioner may aspire to: Sorcerer, Mythographer and Therapist; Sacred Fool and Priest; Artist, Musician and Poet; each may take a lifetime to develop, and a shaman is said to take on all of them while staying a shaman, unlike an artist or therapist who borrows a shamanic element or two. He then treats Sorcerer, Priest/ess, Healer and Mythographer."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Touched by Fire" ;
    dcterms:date "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSorcererRole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sorcerer role"@en, "Rolle des Zauberers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sorcerer deals with spirits and applies their powers to effect change in the world; introduced with a definition of sorcery by Stephen Mace as capturing spirits and harnessing them and ordering one's mental powers to cause inner and outer change."@en ;
    skos:note "Introduced by an epigraph from Stealing the Fire from Heaven by Stephen Mace, whose definition of sorcery is not read through Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSpiritDefined a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "What a spirit is"@en, "Was ein Geist ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "By spirit the author means any non-organic entity with some individuality, ranging from small beings around badly insulated power sockets up to ancient goddesses and gods."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 13; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfRespectSpiritsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Treat spirits with respect and some wariness"@en, "Geister mit Respekt und Vorsicht behandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "As a general rule spirits should be treated respectfully and, where your standing with them is unclear, cautiously, as with strangers or unfamiliar animals; some are shy of humans and others seem mischievous or malicious."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSpiritDefined ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSpiritsAcquirePersona a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits acquire persona by working with humans"@en, "Geister erhalten durch Arbeit mit Menschen eine Persona"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirits are said to lack human-style individuality; by working with humans they gain a persona (name, appearance, sigil, a task) and eventually a life history; fed with energy they grow stronger and may become independent of their creator. Many are said to enjoy doing things for us."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicAoeWorkStrengthensServitor (Aspects of Evocation, 1998): the 1998 node says an elemental servitor grows stronger the more tasks it is given and may develop a character; here spirits in general lack human individuality and acquire a persona (name, appearance, sigil, task) by working with humans, and fed with energy may become independent of their maker."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfResistanceToIllness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enhanced resistance to illness and faster recovery"@en, "Gestärkte Abwehr gegen Krankheit und schnellere Genesung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person's heightened capacity to resist illness and recover sooner, through a spirit made for them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCreatingHealingSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating a healing spirit for a person"@en, "Einen Heilgeist für eine Person erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Create a spirit dedicated to one person whose task is to boost their resistance to an illness and hasten recovery."@en ;
    skos:note "Creation steps not given here; deferred to a later volume."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBServitorsPerformingTasksBehalf (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node lists healing among the tasks servitors carry out; here a spirit is made for a single person to strengthen their fight against an illness, Hine's most frequent spirit work, with no design steps given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingSpiritYieldsRecovery a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Healing spirit yields faster recovery"@en, "Heilgeist ergibt schnellere Genesung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A spirit made for one person is used to strengthen their fight against an illness and to speed their recovery."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCreatingHealingSpirit ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfResistanceToIllness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSpiritsRaiseProbability a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits raise probabilities within what is possible"@en, "Geister erhöhen Wahrscheinlichkeiten im Rahmen des Möglichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spirits are said to be good at raising the likelihood of an outcome provided it is possible in the given situation."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicAoeServitorProbabilityManipulation (Aspects of Evocation, 1998): the 1998 node has a well-used servitor's power to bend probability grow; here any spirit is good at raising likelihood, but only within what the situation makes possible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfClientInactionFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirit working undermined by the client's inaction"@en, "Geistarbeit scheitert an der Untätigkeit des Klienten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A spirit made to help someone find work has much less chance of producing a result if the person has no real wish to seek a job and stays indoors all day."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of a spirit working for a job when the person has no real motivation and stays at home; its chance of a positive result is then much smaller. No deadline; the rate is given only as much less likely; the cause is put on the client's state, which Hine reads as the real problem the working should have aimed at."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAssessingRealProblem a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Assessing the real problem before spirit work"@en, "Vor der Geistarbeit das eigentliche Problem einschätzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before a spirit working, analyse the situation to find its true components (for a job request, perhaps apathy, poor self-belief, or dread of the changes employment would bring) and aim the working at the component most likely to yield."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAssessmentBeforeSpiritWorkPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Assessment before spirit working"@en, "Einschätzung vor Geistarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine holds it necessary to assess a situation before a spirit working, so that the working is aimed at the component where it will be most effective."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAssessingRealProblem ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCreatingHealingSpirit ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "If the real problem lies in apathy, low self-confidence or fear of change, a spirit sent at the stated aim has much less chance of a positive result."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfMakingAmulets a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making amulets"@en, "Herstellung von Amuletten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bind a spirit into an object so that it strengthens some quality, for instance health, courage or good sleep; crystals are currently the most popular base material."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicPrcBCreatingTalismansAmulets (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node links an object with the state of awareness inflamed in ritual and its symbolic associations; here an amulet is an object with a spirit bound into it, made for a quality like health, courage or sleep, mostly on crystals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Amulets, p. 14; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAmuletQualityEnhancement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Amulet-borne enhancement of a quality"@en, "Verstärkung einer Eigenschaft durch ein Amulett"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enhanced health, courage, restful sleep or a similar quality through an amulet carrying a bound spirit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Amulets, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAmuletMakingYieldsQuality a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Amulet making yields enhanced qualities"@en, "Amulettherstellung ergibt verstärkte Eigenschaften"@de ;
    skos:definition "A spirit bound into an object is said to make the amulet strengthen a quality like health, courage or sleep."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfMakingAmulets ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAmuletQualityEnhancement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Amulets, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCounsellingThroughReadings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Problem-solving and counselling through readings"@en, "Problemlösung und Beratung durch Deutungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One-to-one divination sessions said to lead into counselling and problem-solving for the client."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFourSuitTarotBreakdown a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Four-suit tarot problem breakdown"@en, "Problemzerlegung mit den vier Tarotfarben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Analyse with the four tarot suits a client's situation: Wands for ideas and motives, Cups for the overall view or wished-for result, Swords for whether the problem can be split into manageable steps, Disks for the actions to be taken; this may lead into goal-setting, teaching the client to obtain energy or counsel from fitting spirits bound into the cards, identifying coping patterns needing change, and teaching relaxation and centering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTarotBreakdownYieldsCounselling a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tarot breakdown yields problem-solving"@en, "Tarotzerlegung ergibt Problemlösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breaking a problem down by the four suits in one-to-one sessions can lead into counselling and into solving the client's problem."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFourSuitTarotBreakdown ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCounsellingThroughReadings ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTarotSessionsYieldCardSpirits a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tarot sessions yield access to card spirits"@en, "Tarotsitzungen ergeben Zugang zu Kartengeistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "In such sessions the client can be taught to take energy or advice from the spirits bound into the cards."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFourSuitTarotBreakdown ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEnergyFromCardSpirits ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEnergyFromCardSpirits a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing energy or advice from spirits in the cards"@en, "Energie oder Rat von Geistern in den Karten beziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A client, once taught, obtains energy or counsel from spirits said to reside in tarot cards."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDiviningOwnPlace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Divining one's place in a situation"@en, "Den eigenen Platz in einer Situation erdeuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use divination to examine a situation's facets, the people involved, the spirits dominating it and your own role, so as to place yourself and know from where to act, or whether to be involved at all; once your place of power is found, keep to it unless something changes drastically."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCryingShoulderCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming everyone's crying shoulder"@en, "Zur Schulter für alle werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without a found place, one may end up rushing about as everyone's comforter and awake all night; the text contrasts this with influencing events while seeming a bystander."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDiviningOwnPlace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSensingChangeInStreets a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing change while wandering the streets"@en, "Veränderung beim Umherstreifen in den Straßen spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rather than fixing attention on symbols, walk the streets in moments free of thought and notice fleeting clues, such as a gate creaking with a burst of car horns or the shapes of starling flocks over a square; pay attention to coincidences, which are a route to this state."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBNoticingPatternsCoincidence (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node asks one to note hidden patterns and fortuitous coincidences in daily life; here the sensing comes in moments of no-thought while walking city streets, from creaking gates, horns and starling flocks, and coincidence is one route into it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 15; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTruthSenseSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising the truth-sense"@en, "Das Wahrheitsgespür erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With time the practitioner is said to recognise when the truth-sense takes hold and to be ready to gather the fragments, for instance a name, a location, or the likely severity."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of sensing change, in which with time one recognises the truth-sense taking hold and is ready to gather its fragments: a name, a place, the likely severity. The sign is an inner recognition; nothing given checks it against what then happens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPrescience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prescience"@en, "Präkognition / Vorahnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Broad sensing that something is about to happen, which in pure form the author calls prescience."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondADangerSense (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is a prescient sense of impending danger, a byproduct of discipline; here prescience is the pure form of a broad sensing of change in the city that yields fragments such as a name, a place and how bad it will be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfStreetSensingYieldsPrescience a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Street-sensing yields prescience"@en, "Straßenwahrnehmung ergibt Vorahnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Free-floating attention in the streets, with an eye for coincidences, is a route to the broad sensing of change that Hine calls prescience in its pure form."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSensingChangeInStreets ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPrescience ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTwoApproachesToDivination a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two approaches to divination"@en, "Zwei Zugänge zur Divination"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author divides divination into formal symbol systems (Tarot, I Ching, Runes) and free-form methods (black mirrors, pendulums, automatic drawing); spirits may also be used, as familiars living in objects or pictures or roaming freely, or contacted in innerworld trance journeys. He advises using as many methods as possible for a flexible response."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Phil Hine, in Touched by Fire" ;
    dcterms:date "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFindingLostObjects a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding lost objects"@en, "Verlorene Gegenstände finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Locating lost things with a pendulum or with a spirit able to find things reliably; the author once had such a spirit."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondBPendulumWork (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node scans a room with a pendulum to find lost objects; here finding lost things is a capacity Hine regrets lacking at the time, for want of a pendulum or of a spirit that could find them reliably."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Divination, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Staking out the Territory: Sorcerer, Exorcism
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTwoOccasionsForExorcism a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two occasions for exorcism"@en, "Zwei Anlässe für Exorzismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exorcism is said to be needed in two kinds of case: spirits troubling places or objects, and spirits troubling people; haunted dwellings are the commonest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, p. 16; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfGhostBook a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping a ghost book"@en, "Ein Geisterbuch führen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Staff of a haunted hospital ward recorded every uncanny event in a book: the sights, sounds or sensations, the hour, and the part of the ward."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNoTheoryOnlyTactics a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No overall theory, only tactics"@en, "Keine Gesamttheorie, nur Taktiken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says he has no general theory explaining hauntings, only useful tactical approaches."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the method is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfExorcismQuestioning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exorcism assessment by questioning"@en, "Exorzismus-Einschätzung durch Befragung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Begin by asking the clients probing questions: how long the disturbance has lasted; how it shows itself; how many have experienced it; whether it stays in one spot or moves; whether it occurs at certain times; whether the place has a history of this; what the clients believe causes it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 17; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDisturbanceFromDeepMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disturbance sourced in a person's Deep Mind"@en, "Störung mit Ursprung im Tiefen Geist einer Person"@de ;
    skos:definition "A case showed that phenomena blamed on a dead former tenant followed one current tenant from place to place, so their likely source lay in her Deep Mind; a dummy exorcism eased tension in the house while the real work was investigating her, through referral to a magician trained in hypnotherapy."@en ;
    skos:note "Shows why the right questions matter; placebo exorcism is mentioned but not described."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvestigatingHaunting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deeper investigation of a haunting"@en, "Vertiefte Untersuchung eines Spuks"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having gathered details, investigate further: use free-form divination such as a black mirror; spend time in the place noting impressions; if the spirit knocks things about, string thread over objects or doorways; a pendulum hung from a stand can show when something appears; try any trick you think may help."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfQuestioningBeforeInvestigationPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Questioning before deeper investigation"@en, "Befragung vor vertiefter Untersuchung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deeper investigation of a haunting follows once as much detail as possible has been gathered from the clients."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfExorcismQuestioning ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvestigatingHaunting ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfExorcismProcedureSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Exorcism procedure"@en, "Ablauf eines Exorzismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The stages of dealing with a disturbance as Hine sets them out: assessment by questioning the clients, deeper investigation of the place, then, once a presence is established, a decision on what to do and an attempt at contact."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfExorcismQuestioning ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvestigatingHaunting ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfContactingHauntingSpirit ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine orders the handling of a haunting so that each step rests on the one before: questioning the clients gathers the detail on which deeper investigation builds, and only when investigation shows that something is there does one decide what to do and try contact." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, pp. 17-18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPresenceBeforeContactPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Establish a presence before deciding action"@en, "Vor dem Handeln eine Präsenz feststellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only once investigation has shown that something is there does one decide what to do and try to make contact with it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvestigatingHaunting ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfContactingHauntingSpirit ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfZappingSpiritCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not go in zapping"@en, "Nicht mit gezücktem Stab losstürmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Charging in to blast the entity is called the obvious but less sensible option compared with trying contact."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfContactingHauntingSpirit ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfContactingHauntingSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Making contact with the haunting spirit"@en, "Kontakt mit dem spukenden Geist aufnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once something is established as present, decide what to do; rather than attacking it, try to contact the spirit, for example by scrying, remaining receptive to impressions, or bringing along another person as an independent observer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Sorcerer, Exorcism, Assessment, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Staking out the Territory: Priest/ess
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPriestIntercession a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Priest/ess role: intercession"@en, "Rolle des Priesters/der Priesterin: Fürsprache"@de ;
    skos:definition "The priest's main function in any religion is said to be mediating between congregation and divinity, as master or mistress of ceremonies; for the modern shaman this shows as hand-fastings, naming ceremonies, house blessings and initiations, scripted by taste and experience, and as acting as MC at communal gatherings."@en ;
    skos:note "Author jokingly mentions having ordained an Erisian Papess, York's first."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 18; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLeadingEcstaticCeremony a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Leading ecstatic ceremony"@en, "Ekstatische Zeremonie leiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The shaman heads the dancing, or frames a hallucinogen-assisted innerworld journey, guiding others between worlds and opening ways into the inner landscape, the Mythic World; useful skills are drumming, dancing, chants, playing and making instruments, and enthusing groups to drum and chant together."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBCommunalEcstasyMediatingMyth (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node has the magician mediate between everyday life and the community's mythic world; here the shaman as MC leads the dance or frames a hallucinogen-aided journey at drum-ins, solstice gatherings or acid-house parties, with drumming, chant and instrument-making as the skills."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEcstaticCeremonyYieldsEnergy a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ecstatic ceremony yields group energy"@en, "Ekstatische Zeremonie ergibt Gruppenenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Leading drumming, dance or a guided innerworld journey taps group ecstasy, which Hine calls a powerful source of energy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLeadingEcstaticCeremony ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfGroupEcstasyEnergy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfGroupEcstasyEnergy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Group ecstasy as an energy source"@en, "Gruppenekstase als Energiequelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Collective ecstasy is said to generate great energy, to the point that the culture only permits approved outlets."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDrumChantYieldsBonds a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Drum and chant gatherings yield group bonds"@en, "Trommel- und Gesangstreffen ergeben Gruppenbande"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communal drumming and chanting, best begun without visible direction, is said to strengthen bonds, start friendships and raise energy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLeadingEcstaticCeremony, pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNonDirectiveDrumStart ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfStrengthenedGroupBonds ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfStrengthenedGroupBonds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthened group bonds through drumming and chant"@en, "Gestärkte Gruppenbande durch Trommeln und Gesang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Communal drumming and chanting events are said to strengthen bonds, start friendships, raise energy and be enjoyable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDirectingOpenGatheringFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trying to direct an open gathering"@en, "Versuch, ein offenes Treffen zu lenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anyone who tries to organise an open festival gathering into a set ritual is said only to provoke argument and insults; visibly leading is often a bad idea."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of trying to steer an open festival gathering into one sort of ritual, which only brings argument and insults. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the would-be leader's visible direction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNonDirectiveDrumStart a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Non-directive starting of a drum or chant"@en, "Nicht-direktives Anstimmen von Trommel oder Gesang"@de ;
    skos:definition "At an open gathering, for instance around a fire, start a drumbeat or chant, leaving others to join, or allow it to fade if everyone is too far gone; larger events may need more conscious direction and helpers such as other shamans or people acting as spirit-helpers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Intercession, p. 19; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDeathBeliefsConditioning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Death beliefs and bereavement conditioning"@en, "Todesvorstellungen und Konditionierung in der Trauer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beliefs about death (reincarnation, damnation, survival of personality) are said to underpin behaviour and the ego-complex; in bereavement, inherited conditioning reasserts itself as taboo, often making people stay away or deny mourners space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Death, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAgainstPathologisingMourning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against psychiatrists who pathologise long mourning"@en, "Gegen Psychiater, die lange Trauer pathologisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author sarcastically rejects the view of some psychiatrists that mourning longer than average indicates mental breakdown."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed party: psychiatry (some psychiatrists), unnamed."@en, "Entered as a concept: only Hine's side is read; the psychiatrists are neither named nor cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Death, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychopomp a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as psychopomp"@en, "Als Psychopompos wirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conducting a rite that escorts or honours the bodiless spirit of a dead person to its meeting with the keepers of the realm of the dead."@en ;
    skos:note "Rite not described. OCR reads \"10 perform\" for \"To perform\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Death, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFormalCounsellingTraining a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal counselling training"@en, "Formale Beratungsausbildung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking a course in counselling, which Hine thinks probably needed for bereavement work and which he also suggests for those who do not listen well by nature."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator so that the prerequisite of the counselling passage has its two steps as nodes; the text names both steps but describes neither."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Death, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBereavementCounselling a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Bereavement counselling"@en, "Trauerbegleitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Counselling the living after a death, one of the ways the modern shaman meets death beside appearing at funerals and acting as psychopomp; Hine calls it a delicate art and gives no method."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator so that the prerequisite of the counselling passage has its two steps as nodes; the text names both steps but describes neither."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Death, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCounsellingCourseBeforeBereavementPrerequisite a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Counselling training before bereavement counselling"@en, "Beratungsausbildung vor Trauerbegleitung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine thinks some form of course probably in order before one takes up bereavement counselling, because it is a delicate art."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFormalCounsellingTraining ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBereavementCounselling ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Death, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBereavementDelicateCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Bereavement counselling is delicate"@en, "Trauerbegleitung ist heikel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns that bereavement counselling is a delicate skill."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBereavementCounselling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
