pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvocationDefined a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation defined"@en, "Invokation definiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invocation is a set of techniques by which a person identifies with an entity so intensely that some quality or attribute of it appears in them, such as heightened oracular perception or hidden lore; anyone practising magick can develop it, but most do not, so a shaman may be asked to embody an entity at an event or to invoke upon another person."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCInvocation (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node defines invocation as temporary identification with a mythic figure for access to its abilities, a matter of controlled feedback; here it is a battery of techniques the shaman may be asked to perform for others, embodying an entity at an event or invoking upon someone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 20; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfManifestingEntityQualities a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manifesting an entity's qualities"@en, "Die Eigenschaften einer Wesenheit verkörpern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gaining an invoked entity's qualities, e.g. enhanced oracular perception or access to hidden lore, or abilities otherwise lacking, as actors who can sing or dance only in role."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPossessionAndOvershadowing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Possession and overshadowing as degrees of invocation"@en, "Besessenheit und Überschattung als Grade der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Possession is called the extreme degree of invocatory trance, common in shamanic cultures but rare in modern ritual; more usual in Western culture is overshadowing, in which awareness is partly submerged in the entity's; actors absorbed in a role show the same phenomenon."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBOvershadowing (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node spans the states between overshadowing and possession by retained volition and recollection; here possession is the extreme degree, common in shamanic cultures and rare in modern ritual, overshadowing the commoner Western form, and actors absorbed in a role show the same thing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLoaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Loa"@en, "Loa"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entities in Voudoun who ride a Houngan or Mambo and speak through them, supplying answers when the priest seeks hidden knowledge."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Loa" ;
    pm:nameRole "possessing entities that answer questions through Voudoun priests" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvocationYieldsEntityQualities a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation techniques yield entity qualities"@en, "Invokationstechniken ergeben Eigenschaften der Wesenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identifying with an entity through visualisation, speech, gesture, posture and scent makes some quality of it appear in the person."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvocationTechniques ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfManifestingEntityQualities ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInvocationTechniques a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Invocation techniques"@en, "Techniken der Invokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identify with the entity using visualisation, speech, gesture, posture and the other senses, smell especially through incense or essential oils; the same means can be used to invoke upon another person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSpiritsInBodiesAboveLaw a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits in bodies are above the law"@en, "Geister in Körpern stehen über dem Gesetz"@de ;
    skos:definition "In many cultures spirits that wear or ride people are believed exempt from law and free to act in normally unacceptable ways; the shaman partly teaches people how the gods behave."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Priest/ess, Invocation, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Staking out the Territory: Healer
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealerRole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healer role"@en, "Rolle des Heilers"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of the shamanic roles; growing dissatisfaction with allopathic medicine is said to drive people to alternatives. The author adds little to others' writings, stressing that healing is many-levelled."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Healer, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAgainstHealerFixation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against New Age shamanism's focus on healing"@en, "Gegen die Heilungsfixierung des New-Age-Schamanismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says New Age pundits have so stressed the healer role that other shamanic roles are obscured, and that human-growth schools have taken up the glamour of shamanic therapy."@en ;
    skos:note "Disputed party: New Age / human growth shamanism."@en, "Entered as a concept: only Hine's side is read; the New Age writers are neither named nor cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Healer, p. 21; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAttentiveListening a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attentive listening"@en, "Aufmerksames Zuhören"@de ;
    skos:definition "The skill of truly hearing what others say, called a primary skill of any healer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Healer, Listening, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEmptyMindListening a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Listening with an empty mind"@en, "Zuhören mit leerem Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Listen to what someone tells you while keeping your mind clear of thoughts, so your replies do not jump out before you have digested what was said; further practice then develops giving a fitting answer; some may need formal counselling training."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Healer, Listening, p. 22; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEmptyMindListeningYieldsAttention a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Empty-mind listening yields attentive listening"@en, "Zuhören mit leerem Geist ergibt aufmerksames Zuhören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Listening with a blank mind trains what Hine calls a primary skill of every healer, really hearing what is said."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfEmptyMindListening ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAttentiveListening ;
