#
# Staking out the Territory: Mythographer
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfMythographerRole a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mythographer role"@en, "Rolle des Mythographen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Called perhaps the most important shamanic role: one who keeps, interprets and extends the community's pool of myth; myths are said to be continually rewritten, destroyed and recovered, a felt connection to them sustains continuity and stability as social change speeds up, and in our culture the role is largely carried by literature and film."@en ;
    skos:note "The sentence on continuity and stability was carried only by the second extraction pass and is folded in here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Mythographer, pp. 24-25; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCampbellNewMyths a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Joseph Campbell on the need for new myths"@en, "Joseph Campbell über den Bedarf an neuen Mythen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Campbell is reported to have said society badly needs new myths; the author qualifies that modern myths are not lacking but fragmented."@en ;
    skos:note "Campbell is cited without a work; the qualification is Hine's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Mythographer, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLivingMythAbsorbsModern a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living myth absorbs the modern"@en, "Lebendiger Mythos nimmt das Moderne auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Aboriginal people are said to dream of cars and jets, holding these always existed in the Dreamtime; tribal shamans translate Western icons into their myth pools to soften the shock of meeting technology; Westerners meanwhile dig up dead cultures' myths and project their fantasies onto them, neglecting the near future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Staking out the Territory, Mythographer, p. 24; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Social Wounds
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCityAsLivingEntity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The city as a living entity"@en, "Die Stadt als lebendes Wesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cities are said to be easier to grasp if regarded as living beings, vast intricate systems housing us as one organism among many; they breed spirits ranging from very real demons (poverty, frustration, despair) to elementals arising from cable tangles and heavy industry; the experience of generations becomes embedded in a city's collective psyche."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcBSpiritsEverywhereHabitsTechnologiesCities (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node lists urban spirits among the entities beyond classical terms; here the city itself is to be regarded as a living entity whose collective psyche holds the experience of generations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSensingCityPulse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing a city's pulse and moods"@en, "Puls und Stimmungen einer Stadt spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving how a city changes with the seasons and responds to its residents' moods, and the moods and histories settled in its districts; Hine says getting the feel of a city takes time, to grow roots and feelers, and that much of the awareness grows with familiarity."@en ;
    skos:note "The time needed to put down roots, entered by the first pass as a prerequisite without a prior step, is folded in here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 26; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerBoundToTerritory a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic power bound to territory"@en, "Schamanische Kraft an ein Gebiet gebunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Among non-industrial peoples the power of a shamanic practitioner may be tied to a territory, a village or sacred ground; Hine says that after three years in Leeds he begins to feel such affection and affinity for the city as an entity, though he knows only a small part of it well."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLeedsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Leeds as an entity"@en, "Leeds als Wesenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The city of Leeds, which the author after three years' residence feels growing affinity and affection for as an entity in itself."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Leeds" ;
    pm:nameRole "the city considered as a living being" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWanderingCityAnimalForm a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Wandering the city in animal form, then on foot"@en, "Die Stadt in Tiergestalt, dann zu Fuß durchstreifen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Send your awareness through the streets in cat or bird shape, travelling an inner map of the city held in your head; afterwards walk the districts in person, feeling for the prevailing moods and histories deposited like sediment beneath them."@en ;
    skos:note "The order is inner wandering first, then the walk through the districts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCityWanderingYieldsCitySense a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "City wandering yields city-sensing"@en, "Stadtstreifzug ergibt Stadtgespür"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting awareness roam the city in animal shape and then walking its districts lets Hine feel for its moods and histories."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWanderingCityAnimalForm ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfSensingCityPulse ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfScarredPlaces a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Scarred places"@en, "Vernarbte Orte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Areas can be wounded by disaster (Hillsborough) or economic decline, the wound permeating the whole area; the author asks whether such scars might be healed even slightly; estates built over battle sites show high psychic turbulence such as UFO and ghost reports and untenantable houses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 27; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDerelictAreasStrangeBeings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Derelict areas and strange beings"@en, "Verlassene Gegenden und seltsame Wesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disused areas are said often to coincide with appearances of strange beings, an observation the author says is supported by accounts in a book by John Keel."@en ;
    skos:note "A book by John Keel (spelled Keele in the text layer) on strange creatures is named as seeming to confirm the observation; the book is not read through Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Social Wounds: Community
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCommunityDefined a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Community defined"@en, "Gemeinschaft definiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the author community arises from belonging to a network of relations whose members share concerns and viewpoints and collude to keep them, from survival matters to subtle norms of interaction; communities are more complex than assumed and members rarely share all views. Beyond work with individuals he has begun workings for whole communities, as a tribal shaman does for a tribe."@en ;
    skos:note "OCR \"social 82418\" probably reads \"social gaffes\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Community, p. 28; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Social Wounds: Furies and The Scream
#

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Furies ritual"@en, "Das Ritual der Furien"@de ;
    skos:definition "During the 1989 heat-wave, with rising violence against women and homophobia in the area, a group raised an intensely focused energy vortex that let the Furies enter the shared consciousness of the women of Leeds; the women taking part voiced and directed their anger at oppressive male behaviour into the rite instead of holding it in."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Furies"@en, "Die Furien"@de ;
    skos:definition "A group of female spirits from Greek myth whose action is to restrain oppressive men."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the Furies" ;
    pm:nameRole "female spirits that constrain oppressive males" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesRitualYieldsRelease a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Furies rite yields release of anger"@en, "Furienritual ergibt Freisetzung der Wut"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Furies rite let the women involved voice and direct their anger at oppressive men, which is said to be healing in itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingReleaseOfAnger ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingReleaseOfAnger a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing release of anger"@en, "Heilsame Freisetzung von Wut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Articulating and directing anger outward into a rite, which is said to be healing in itself and to relieve the stress of repression."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Women resisting oppressors; incidents fell"@en, "Frauen wehrten sich; Vorfälle gingen zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the following weeks the group heard of several women turning on men who oppressed them, and local incidents decreased."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, not as a sign announced in advance: in the weeks after the Furies working the group heard of several women turning on men who oppressed them, and the local incidents dropped. The reports reached the group by hearsay, and no count or comparison with the end of the heat-wave is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTheScream a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Scream"@en, "Der Schrei"@de ;
    skos:definition "An anger-channelling exercise from the Furies working: imagine being all women of every culture, land and era, of every face and race, gathering their anger at oppression and crying out that they have had enough and will take no more."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfScreamYieldsFreeEnergy a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Scream yields free energy"@en, "Der Schrei ergibt freie Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anger raised in the Scream and aimed at no particular person becomes free energy that can be directed magically."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTheScream ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFreeEnergyPureWill ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFreeEnergyPureWill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free energy / pure Will"@en, "Freie Energie / reiner Wille"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anger not aimed at particular people is said to become free energy or pure Will that can be magically directed, sending a ripple through the group's collective psyche; it also shows the power of focused will to effect change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfScreamYieldsRelease a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Scream yields release of stress"@en, "Der Schrei ergibt Stressabbau"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redirecting anger through the Scream is said to release energy otherwise held in the BodyMind as stress and frustration."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTheScream ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHealingReleaseOfAnger ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 29; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesExhaustionCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The Furies rite exhausted its workers"@en, "Das Furienritual erschöpfte die Beteiligten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author reports the rite nearly wrecked all participants and took months to recover from, though they judged it worthwhile."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-warning: the cost of the author's own working, which the group judged worth it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesRitual ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWorkingWithSituations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Working with situations rather than individuals"@en, "Mit Situationen statt mit Einzelnen arbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Traditional magick is said to aim at changing one person or one aspect; the author is working instead with whole situations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInterveningInSituation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Intervening magically in an evolving situation"@en, "Magisches Eingreifen in eine sich entwickelnde Lage"@de ;
    skos:definition "Look without bias at the elements of a developing situation, divine its probable outcomes, and decide when and above all how to intervene magically, if intervention is needed at all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfHangingBackCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Heed the urge to hang back"@en, "Dem Drang zum Zurückhalten folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When he unaccountably holds back from a situation, following that intuition usually reveals why involvement, at least in the first-proposed manner, is unwise; waiting until more information arrives is often wiser, since rushing in can make matters worse."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInterveningInSituation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Social Wounds, Furies, The Scream, p. 30; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# MAGI-PROP
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfReichMythPolitics a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reich on myth and politics"@en, "Reich über Mythos und Politik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wilhelm Reich is reported to have observed that the Left lacked mass appeal by offering only intellectual, material answers without a total reality as backdrop, while fascists grasped the need for a mythological dimension; the author adds that social reality is manipulated by appeal to the mythic world, as Nazi use of symbol and myth showed."@en ;
    skos:note "Reich is cited without a work; the extension to Nazi symbolism is Hine's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFarRightUnconsciousMagic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Far-right groups as unconscious magicians"@en, "Rechtsextreme Gruppen als unbewusste Magier"@de ;
    skos:definition "The British Nationalist Party is said to be aware of magick, if unconsciously, and mimetic, extending into any emotive cause that feeds it; it is reinforced by the meme of xenophobia and its mutation, anti-intellectualism; history breeds mythic images and symbols keep power against a mythological backdrop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, p. 31; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# MAGI-PROP: Word Viruses
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWordVirus a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Word Virus"@en, "Wortvirus"@de ;
    skos:definition "A word virus is a minute verbal or visual unit which traps its human host's energy into repeating an instruction or behaviour; adverts, jingles, gossip and political ideas sustaining power relations carry it; attitudes such as getting even, being right or clinging to power can be understood magically as viral entities, hard to counter by argument alone. Gandhi is cited for the view that attitudes, not people, are the problem."@en ;
    skos:note "Gandhi is named for the view that the problem is attitudes rather than people, without a work."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicPrcAVirusSystems (Prime Chaos, 1999): the 1999 node gives the general model of a virus as an instruction set that makes its host replicate it; here the word virus is the political form, attitudes such as getting even or holding on to power taken as viral entities that argument alone barely shifts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Word Viruses, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCounteringWordViruses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A developing approach to counter word viruses"@en, "Ein sich entwickelnder Ansatz gegen Wortviren"@de ;
    skos:definition "A magical approach is said to be developing to fight these viruses head-on, either replacing or backing up other counter-strategies; magick has been tied to the political struggle for freedom since the seventeenth century."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on fixity: approach described as still developing. OCR \"18\" for \"is\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Word Viruses, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfGroundZeroPolitics a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Political magick as ground-zero politics"@en, "Politische Magie als Politik von Grund auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Political magick for the author means surviving oppressive institutions and viruses; the earliest Heal the Earth rite drew on a book by Starhawk (Dreaming the Dark) that joins politics and magic to regain power without repeating oppressors' power-games; individual empowerment and pooled energy are key."@en ;
    skos:note "Starhawk, Dreaming the Dark, is named as the inspiration of the first working of Heal the Earth; the book is not read through Hine."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Word Viruses, p. 32; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNewPoliticalVirusesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not breed new political viruses"@en, "Keine neuen politischen Viren züchten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Collective magical politics must avoid spawning new viruses that in time harden into structures as repressive as those they oppose."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfGroundZeroPolitics ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Word Viruses, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# MAGI-PROP: Out Demon Out; Pagans Against the Poll Tax
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCursingIndividualsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Cursing individuals undermines yourself"@en, "Das Verfluchen Einzelner untergräbt einen selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cursing is called dubious ground: for anyone holding to free will, seeking power over another person is contradictory and devalues oneself; most curses the author has met stem from petty quarrels and wishes to control changed situations."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-warning against a method the book later discusses."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondBAgainstCondemningCurses (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node disputes the view that cursing is wrong; here Hine calls the cursing of individuals dubious and self-devaluing for anyone holding to free will, while granting it validity among the repressed and turning to curses on institutions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCursingAmongOppressed ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCursingAmongOppressed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cursing among the oppressed; cursing institutions"@en, "Fluchen bei Unterdrückten; Institutionen verfluchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cursing is said to be accepted in some cultures and most developed among peoples repressed by stronger groups who lack other means to recover power; some feminist writers have explored binding rapists; modern practice has turned to cursing institutions rather than individuals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfMoneyAsEnergyTransfer a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Money as energy transfer"@en, "Geld als Energieübertragung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The basis of the Poll Tax curse: handing over money counts as a transfer of energy, heavily charged, being a root of society; computers are said to be especially sensitive to magically generated interference."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBuyingWarts a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Buying warts"@en, "Warzen abkaufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A trick of old wart-charmers: buy the warts from the sufferer and transfer them elsewhere."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBuyingWartsYieldsRemoval a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Buying warts yields wart removal"@en, "Warzenkauf ergibt Warzenentfernung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Buying warts from the sufferer is the old charmer's way of moving them elsewhere."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBuyingWarts ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWartRemoval ;
