pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWartRemoval a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wart removal"@en, "Warzenentfernung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting rid of warts by transferring them away."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPollTaxChequeCurse a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Poll Tax blank-cheque curse"@en, "Blankoscheck-Fluch gegen die Kopfsteuer"@de ;
    skos:definition "From an anonymous circulated document: take a blank cheque, sign it with a magickal persona, write suitable sigils in place of a sum, and so pay the targeted authority a problem that will hinder Poll Tax collection, e.g. half a year of computer faults; posting the cheque activates the curse."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInstitutionalDisruption a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disrupting an institution's operations"@en, "Störung des Betriebs einer Institution"@de ;
    skos:definition "Causing troubles such as computer failure that impede an authority's work, here Poll Tax collection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 33; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTelevisionDisruptionOutcome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magicians claim to have disrupted TV transmissions"@en, "Magier behaupten, Fernsehübertragungen gestört zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "One group of magicians claimed to have briefly interfered with television broadcasts."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as an outcome report, not as a sign announced in advance: a group of magicians claimed to have disrupted television transmissions for a moment; Hine reports the claim at second hand, without its source or any check."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfChequeCurseYieldsDisruption a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Blank-cheque curse yields institutional disruption"@en, "Blankoscheck-Fluch ergibt Störung der Institution"@de ;
    skos:definition "The posted cheque is meant to pay the authority a problem, such as months of computer trouble, that disrupts the collection of the tax."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPollTaxChequeCurse ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInstitutionalDisruption ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPoliticalCursingObjectionsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Arguments against political cursing"@en, "Einwände gegen politisches Fluchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against such acts it is argued that one may not have the right, and that they will reinforce the public image of pagans and occultists as evil; the author leaves it to individual judgement while noting that suffering repression helplessly wears people down fast."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPollTaxChequeCurse ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfFuriesAsCurse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Furies working as a curse"@en, "Die Furienarbeit als Fluch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Furies working can be seen as a curse aimed at violence and at the oppression of one social group by another, an extreme response to an extreme situation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfArgumentAloneFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Argument alone fails against viruses and fortresses"@en, "Argumente allein versagen gegen Viren und Festungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Viral attitudes are said to be hard to defeat through reasoning or emotional appeals on their own, and some fortresses of fixed belief cannot be taken apart by reason and gentle persuasion, which is offered as the case for magical counter-action."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of countering viral attitudes and fortresses of fixed belief by rational or emotional argument alone. No deadline; the rate is given as sometimes; the cause is put on the entrenched structure, and Hine offers this as the case for magical counter-action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychicAssaultOnFortresses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Psychic assault on fortresses of belief"@en, "Psychischer Angriff auf Festungen des Glaubens"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one curses at all, it is held better to target oppressive structures and ideas and the demons of fear and hatred; growth may require destroying the psychic structures by which an entity confines itself, fortresses of dogma that argument cannot dismantle, by finding a back way in and showing the occupants the demons they have disowned."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 34; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfInnerDemonsUnpleasantCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Confronting inner demons is unpleasant"@en, "Die Konfrontation mit inneren Dämonen ist unangenehm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Facing one's inner demons, willingly or not, is never pleasant, though part of growth."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPsychicAssaultOnFortresses ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), MAGI-PROP, Out Demon Out, Pagans Against the Poll Tax, p. 35; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Looking to the Future?
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTechniquesContinuallyUpdated a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Shamanic techniques are continually updated"@en, "Schamanische Techniken werden ständig weiterentwickelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanism is called the oldest magical practice; its techniques are stressed to be under constant updating as people arrive from different backgrounds; it is said to hold an effective psycho-technology and positive life ethic and to be adaptable."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how fixed the methods are."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Looking to the Future?, p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfShamanLabelGlamourCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sanitising and the glamour of the shaman label"@en, "Verharmlosung und der Glanz des Schamanentitels"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author fears shamanic techniques are being sanitised as self-improvement manuals edge out the magical essentials; he is wary of people quick to call themselves shamans and does not see himself as one, calling it a glamour to avoid."@en ;
    skos:note "Self-warning: Hine declines the label of shaman for himself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTechniquesContinuallyUpdated ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Looking to the Future?, p. 36; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCommonEssentialsAcrossSystems a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Common essentials across systems"@en, "Gemeinsame Grundlagen der Systeme"@de ;
    skos:definition "The core of magical experience and practice is held to be alike whatever symbols clothe them, so mastering one approach eases learning another; the author regards separate traditions as belonging to a past age and, like his occupational therapy training, picks the most effective techniques per situation; since no single person can fill every role, dialogue and self-assessment among practitioners are needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:ChaosMagicCondASelfAssessment (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node is the practice of examining one's own behaviour with dispassion; here assessing oneself and the techniques one wields is one need of a shamanic practice that draws on many systems and many practitioners."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Looking to the Future?, p. 37; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Postscript
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNoSystemNoTeacher a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No system and no teacher"@en, "Kein System und kein Lehrer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says the book reflects his own uses of shamanic techniques, that he is not building a definite system, and that he does not regard himself as a teacher of them."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on fixity of method."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Postscript, p. 38; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Appendices: Activate The Bear
#

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerAndItsCost a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power and its cost"@en, "Macht und ihr Preis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Power is said to be hard to find and to hold, to create tensions and to come only at great cost; it makes demands so that one can make demands back, balance lying in a rough equal trade; there are few fixed rules and no easy roads to it; defining it diminishes it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondASacrificeForPowerCautela (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node makes alienation and sacrifice the price of each gain of power; here the demands of power are met by a rough equal trade-off, and power has few fixed rules and is lessened by definition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerAttractsMothsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Power attracts takers and givers"@en, "Macht zieht Nehmer und Geber an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Power makes one visible like a candle among moths: people will either try to strip it from you or hand theirs over to you; both are unpleasant and insidious, and some are addicted to either."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerAndItsCost ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfChasingPower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Chasing power"@en, "Der Macht nachjagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One has to go after power to show it one is in earnest; the means hardly matter, and Hine names a nine-day hanging on the world-tree or lying under the stars while a near-overdose of home-made amphetamine works on the brain; there is no easy road and no free ride."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it. Named as a path without steps; the cautions and the failure of this section point at it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfExtremePowerRoutesFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Most who chase power by extreme means do not survive"@en, "Die meisten, die Macht auf extremen Wegen suchen, überleben nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Of those who seek power through near-fatal routes, the author says most fail to come through, Fuller being a lucky exception."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of chasing power by near-fatal routes, which most do not survive; Buckminster Fuller is the lucky exception. No deadline; the rate is the word most; the cause is put on the danger of the route itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfExtremePowerRoutesCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Extreme ways of chasing power often kill"@en, "Extreme Wege der Machtsuche enden oft tödlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must pursue power to prove sincerity, by whatever means (hanging on the world-tree, a near-overdose); Buckminster Fuller found it on the brink of suicide and survived, but most who try such routes do not."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfChasingPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerCorruptsEnvious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power corrupts the envious as well as the holder"@en, "Macht verdirbt auch die Neider"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking up the old saying that power corrupts, Hine asks whom it corrupts and answers: not only those who hold it but also those who envy them, being too idle or too afraid to pursue it themselves."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the integrator from the reading of the whole text; no extraction record carries it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 40; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAgainstImpeccableWarrior a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against spiritual purists and the impeccable warrior"@en, "Gegen spirituelle Puristen und den makellosen Krieger"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author attacks abstaining people who claim to have conquered the ego as psychic fascism, and rejects the impeccable-warrior ideal; after an acquaintance who offered him Russian roulette died two days later from a mine, he says anyone calling himself a warrior will meet something sharp."@en ;
    skos:note "Target is the impeccable-warrior ideal of the Castaneda tradition, which is not named in the text."@en, "Entered as a concept: only Hine's side is read; the warrior ideal he rejects is not cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNoEasyRouteToPowerFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No easy route to power"@en, "Kein leichter Weg zur Macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting gains without pain, hoping for a shortcut, or clinging to the safety of light and barriers is said not to bring power; there is no free ride to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of seeking power without pain, by a shortcut, or from the shelter of bright light and barriers. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the seeker's unwillingness to pay its cost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBlackMagicianLabelCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Using power earns the label Black Magician"@en, "Wer Macht gebraucht, gilt als Schwarzmagier"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hine warns that the use of power is harder than its pursuit: someone will always call the user a Black Magician, above all one who keeps asking awkward questions; he tells of an acquaintance who rang to ask whether Hine had been cursing him."@en ;
    skos:note "Added in the reconciliation of the two extraction passes: only the second pass carried it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerAndItsCost ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPanNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Pan"@en, "Pan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Invoked by the author and Vishvanath at Beltane dawn in the Leeds green belt with cheap wine as libation; nothing further is said of him."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicCondCPanNaming (Condensed Chaos, 1995): the 1995 node makes Pan the god of sudden illumination and creative derangement; here Pan is only invoked with a cheap libation at a Beltane dawn in the Leeds green belt, and nothing more is said of him."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Pan" ;
    pm:nameRole "god invoked at Beltane" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 41; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDuckingPowerCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ducking power diminishes and burns"@en, "Macht ausweichen schwächt und verletzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once power finds you, evading it only diminishes you and may hurt others unawares; power brings responsibilities and sorrows."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPowerAndItsCost ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfDefiningPowerFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Defining power loses it"@en, "Macht zu definieren heißt, sie zu verlieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "To pin power down in a definition is said to diminish it until it is gone."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of grasping power by defining it, which lessens it until it is lost. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the act of definition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfUnanswerableQuestionsFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unanswerable questions bring stasis of will"@en, "Unbeantwortbare Fragen führen zum Stillstand des Willens"@de ;
    skos:definition "An epigraph says that asking questions without answers leaves the soul at a crossroads of wavering, so that searching for wisdom yields only a halted will."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of a search for wisdom pursued through questions that have no answer, which ends only in a stasis of will. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the seeker's vacillation."@en, "The epigraph is ascribed to an Adeptus Astartes proverb, a fictional source; Hine prints it without comment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, Activate The Bear: It's A Teenage Rampage!, p. 42; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .




#
# Appendices: TimeWind
