pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfRidingStormSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Riding a storm-spirit into shaman-time"@en, "Einen Sturmgeist in die Schamanenzeit reiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sit in silence during a storm, catch a glimpse of a storm-spirit, give it a name, and ride it into shaman-time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfAzgNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Azg"@en, "Azg"@de ;
    skos:definition "A storm-spirit glimpsed during a storm and named by the author, which he rode into shaman-time and which tears words from his throat."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Azg" ;
    pm:nameRole "storm-spirit" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfRidingStormSpiritYieldsShamanTime a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Riding the storm-spirit yields shaman-time"@en, "Ritt auf dem Sturmgeist ergibt Schamanenzeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Riding the storm-spirit Azg took Hine into shaman-time."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfRidingStormSpirit ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfShamanTime ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfTimeWindReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "TimeWind written after riding a storm-spirit"@en, "TimeWind nach dem Reiten eines Sturmgeistes geschrieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says he glimpsed a storm-spirit, named it Azg, rode it into shaman-time, and on returning the words of the essay flowed out by themselves."@en ;
    skos:note "The text says the words flowed of themselves; that Azg spoke them is implied at most."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Phil Hine" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "No speaker is named; the words are said to have flowed of themselves after the author rode the storm-spirit Azg into shaman-time" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Late one night while a storm raged round the house, sitting in silence, after briefly glimpsing a storm-spirit that Hine named Azg; the words began on his leaving shaman-time." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfGnosisBeyondWords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gnosis cannot be carried by words"@en, "Gnosis lässt sich nicht durch Worte übermitteln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shamanic magick is said to rest on personal Gnosis, knowledge of the heart, which wells from the Deep Mind or strikes like lightning and can only be felt or half-glimpsed; words give only second-hand light and imprison the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfWordHeavinessFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being word-heavy prevents the dance"@en, "Wortschwere verhindert den Tanz"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says that when weighed down by words he cannot dance until the storm sweeps them off; words are said to imprison the body and hide the dance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: of the dance when the shaman is heavy with words; Hine cannot dance until the storm whirls them away. No deadline or rate; the cause is put on the words, which imprison the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfStagesOfLanguageSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of language from gesture to words"@en, "Stufen der Sprache von der Geste zum Wort"@de ;
    skos:definition "The forms of expression in the order Hine gives them: gesture and the body first, then poetry, then the pictorial image, and now a life among words in which bodily language has become mysterious."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPhysicalLanguage ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPoetryStage ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPictorialImageStage ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLivingAmongstWords ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Hine gives the forms of expression in the order in which they arose: shamanism born first of gesture and the body, then poetry of rhythm and cadence, then pictures and glyphs, and now a life among words; each later stage is measured by its distance from the first, whose bodily language now seems mysterious." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPhysicalLanguage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stage 1: physical language"@en, "Stufe 1: Körpersprache"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gesture and the twisting of the body, said to address the Deep Mind directly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPoetryStage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stage 2: poetry"@en, "Stufe 2: Poesie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rhythm and cadence; poetry as motion, image, sound, dance and music."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfPictorialImageStage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stage 3: pictorial image"@en, "Stufe 3: Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Glyphs, symbols and picture-writing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfLivingAmongstWords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stage 4: living amongst words"@en, "Stufe 4: Leben unter Worten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The present, where words bind us into Time and make tradition possible as linear transmission."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfReadingWordlessKnowledge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading wordless knowledge in chance patterns"@en, "Wortloses Wissen in zufälligen Mustern lesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the storm-spirit has torn his words away, Hine reads knowledge that has no words in ordinary patterns: an iron gate rattling, rain sprayed across a window pane, a dull toothache."@en ;
    skos:note "Added in the reconciliation of the two extraction passes: only the second pass carried it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 43; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfShamanTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Entering shaman-time"@en, "In die Schamanenzeit eintreten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state of cyclic, non-linear time without gods, mapped paths or systems, outside the spirals of ordinary Time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfNamelessGuidesOneBook a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Nameless guides and the one book"@en, "Namenlose Führer und das eine Buch"@de ;
    skos:definition "In shaman-time guides are nameless and formless, half-glimpsed; any names are titles one must be clever enough to offer them, at the risk of their wild laughter; the only book is the world, which each must learn to read."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfOutDancingTeacherSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The pupil out-dances the teacher"@en, "Die Schülerin übertanzt den Lehrer"@de ;
    skos:definition "A pupil is said always to recognise her readiness once her dancing surpasses her teacher's."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: of the pupil, who recognises her readiness once her dancing surpasses the teacher's. The sign is given in the figure of the essay and is not tied to any stated exercise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCarriedOutsideTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being carried outside Time by the dance"@en, "Durch den Tanz aus der Zeit getragen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The dance may carry the dancer outside the spirals of Time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBreakingWordAddictionYieldsRelease a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking word addiction yields release from Time"@en, "Durchbrechen der Wortsucht ergibt Befreiung aus der Zeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breaking the cycle of addiction to words is how one lets the dance carry one outside the spirals of Time."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBreakingWordAddiction ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicTmsTbfCarriedOutsideTime ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TouchedByFire ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Touched by Fire: Techniques of Modern Shamanism Volume 3 (Pagan News Publication, 1989; Acrobat conversion of March 1998), Appendices, TimeWind, p. 44; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item techniques-of-modern-shamanism-vol-1-2-and-3-by-phil-hine-collection, file Hine, Phil - Techniques of Modern Shamanism vol 3_djvu.txt" .

pmp:ChaosMagicTmsTbfBreakingWordAddiction a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Breaking the habit of words"@en, "Den Suchtkreislauf der Worte durchbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To be carried out of Time's spirals by the dance, break the habitual cycle of dependence on words, because words cannot enter space, and dancing requires space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
